262
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:22,001
- [Man] The Tougars!

263
00:09:22,001 --> 00:09:23,609
- [Servo] Oh, they spent a
lot of money on a fortress,

264
00:09:23,609 --> 00:09:24,502
but no gate!

265
00:09:24,502 --> 00:09:26,158
(Crow chuckling)

266
00:09:26,158 --> 00:09:27,701
- [Crow] Man, this movie is already

267
00:09:27,701 --> 00:09:28,981
50 times more expensive

268
00:09:28,981 --> 00:09:32,177
than all the movies
we've seen put together!

269
00:09:32,177 --> 00:09:33,927
- [Servo] The chores!

270
00:09:36,851 --> 00:09:38,101
Come on, honey.

271
00:09:39,073 --> 00:09:40,627
There you go.

272
00:09:40,627 --> 00:09:43,112
- [Crow] Hey, no one
invited me to the pillaging.

273
00:09:43,112 --> 00:09:44,757
- Hey, you be cursed, murdering scum!

274
00:09:44,757 --> 00:09:45,663
- [Crow] Go girl.

275
00:09:45,663 --> 00:09:46,985
Right on, woman!

276
00:09:46,985 --> 00:09:47,818
(exciting music)

277
00:09:47,818 --> 00:09:49,005
(maniacal laughter)

278
00:09:49,005 --> 00:09:52,926
- She will make quite a tasty
dish to take to our chief.

279
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:54,738
- [Crow] I'm not that tasty.

280
00:09:54,738 --> 00:09:56,161
I'm mostly grizzle!

281
00:09:56,161 --> 00:09:57,916
- There's a caravan! (mumbles)

282
00:09:57,916 --> 00:09:59,562
(shouting, clamoring)

283
00:09:59,562 --> 00:10:00,552
- [Servo] Hey, watch the hands.

284
00:10:00,552 --> 00:10:01,454
Don't get fresh.

285
00:10:01,454 --> 00:10:02,957
(women screaming)

286
00:10:02,957 --> 00:10:05,444
- [Mike] Let Pat Carroll go, you beast.

287
00:10:05,444 --> 00:10:07,004
(women screaming)

288
00:10:07,004 --> 00:10:08,829
- [Servo] Dan Haggerty!

289
00:10:08,829 --> 00:10:10,206
- These hands I cannot lift to help them.

290
00:10:10,206 --> 00:10:12,473
- [Mike] I bowled last
night and I'm pretty stiff.

291
00:10:12,473 --> 00:10:13,408
(exciting music)

292
00:10:13,408 --> 00:10:14,977
- [Crow] Wagons east!

293
00:10:14,977 --> 00:10:18,270
(Servo mumbling)

294
00:10:18,270 --> 00:10:21,845
- [Servo] Hey, the caterers are here!

295
00:10:21,845 --> 00:10:24,512
(Servo singing)

296
00:10:27,064 --> 00:10:29,568
- [Crow] This is not the shortcut!

297
00:10:29,568 --> 00:10:31,538
(crashing)

298
00:10:31,538 --> 00:10:32,371
Dr. Who!

299
00:10:34,364 --> 00:10:35,765
(horses whinnying)

300
00:10:35,765 --> 00:10:39,919
At long last, our nation says
no to renaissance festivals.

301
00:10:39,919 --> 00:10:43,002
Finn ropin' here at the Mongol rodeo.

302
00:10:44,645 --> 00:10:45,960
- Spare me, I beg you!

303
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,701
- [Soldier] Come closer,
my blubbering one,

304
00:10:47,701 --> 00:10:49,310
and let me take a look at you.

305
00:10:49,310 --> 00:10:50,716
You seem to be well-fed.

306
00:10:50,716 --> 00:10:52,255
You're heavy enough.

307
00:10:52,255 --> 00:10:54,075
- [Man] Oh, please spare me, sire.

308
00:10:54,075 --> 00:10:56,953
I'll do anything you wish, anything.

309
00:10:56,953 --> 00:10:58,196
- [Crow] Wash my car.

310
00:10:58,196 --> 00:10:59,927
And pick up Tina from piano lessons.

311
00:10:59,927 --> 00:11:02,224
- Swear you'll serve me.
(man moaning)

312
00:11:02,224 --> 00:11:03,586
- [Man] Yes, sire.

313
00:11:03,586 --> 00:11:04,948
I will, I will.

314
00:11:04,948 --> 00:11:06,558
You can have anything I own.

315
00:11:06,558 --> 00:11:07,808
Here, see this?

316
00:11:09,876 --> 00:11:11,911
- [Crow] A finger towel, great!

317
00:11:11,911 --> 00:11:12,744
(soldier laughing maniacally)

318
00:11:12,744 --> 00:11:13,577
- [Mike] And here's a soap sliver.

319
00:11:13,577 --> 00:11:14,799
Please spare my life.

320
00:11:14,799 --> 00:11:17,780
- Listen well, son of misery.

321
00:11:17,780 --> 00:11:20,609
- [Servo] You know my dad?

322
00:11:20,609 --> 00:11:21,702
- Send this to us

323
00:11:21,702 --> 00:11:23,347
as a signal to Chief Kalin

324
00:11:23,347 --> 00:11:26,005
that the prince's soldiers
have left the city.

325
00:11:26,005 --> 00:11:29,731
I shall await your signal
at the river in seven moons.

326
00:11:29,731 --> 00:11:30,761
Now, hear me,

327
00:11:30,761 --> 00:11:32,482
oh miserable one.
- [Crow] Danny Kaye!

328
00:11:32,482 --> 00:11:33,776
- If you fail us.

329
00:11:33,776 --> 00:11:36,390
If you deceive us, you
shall die like a dog!

330
00:11:36,390 --> 00:11:40,701
(Crow emulating dog yelping)

331
00:11:40,701 --> 00:11:42,007
(sad music)

332
00:11:42,007 --> 00:11:44,048
- [Voiceover] This was a
time of giants and dragons.

333
00:11:44,048 --> 00:11:44,944
- [Mike] And low inflation.

334
00:11:44,944 --> 00:11:46,546
- [Voiceover] When brave and fearless men

335
00:11:46,546 --> 00:11:48,182
rose up to perform mighty deeds

336
00:11:48,182 --> 00:11:49,845
against the forces of evil.

337
00:11:49,845 --> 00:11:50,728
- [Servo] I'm Mike Wallace.

338
00:11:50,728 --> 00:11:53,115
- [Voiceover] Mightiest
of all was Invincor,

339
00:11:53,115 --> 00:11:55,284
mighty defender of the righteous.

340
00:11:55,284 --> 00:11:56,241
- [Crow] And a nice guy.

341
00:11:56,241 --> 00:11:57,545
- [Voiceover] Who raised his magic sword

342
00:11:57,545 --> 00:11:58,835
across the breadth of the land,

343
00:11:58,835 --> 00:12:01,847
to smite the enemies of the just.

344
00:12:01,847 --> 00:12:03,119
- [Mike] Riding Lori Barbero.

345
00:12:03,119 --> 00:12:03,952
- [Voiceover] After many years,

346
00:12:03,952 --> 00:12:07,044
when Invincor had grown weary with age,

347
00:12:07,044 --> 00:12:09,050
his tasks were done.

348
00:12:09,050 --> 00:12:11,583
- [Servo] He was given a
farewell banquet and a small TV.

349
00:12:11,583 --> 00:12:13,447
- [Voiceover] As he traveled far and wide,

350
00:12:13,447 --> 00:12:15,200
o ye wandering pilgrims.

351
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:16,076
- [Servo] Uh, boss.

352
00:12:16,076 --> 00:12:18,292
- [Voiceover] Think of the young man.

353
00:12:18,292 --> 00:12:19,648
- [Servo] Hey, boss.

354
00:12:19,648 --> 00:12:21,475
- [Voiceover] Stout of
heart, strong of arm,

355
00:12:21,475 --> 00:12:22,889
and brave of spirit.

356
00:12:22,889 --> 00:12:24,109
- [Crow] And taut of buttocks.

357
00:12:24,109 --> 00:12:26,835
- [Voiceover] And when you
find such a man, give him this.

358
00:12:26,835 --> 00:12:30,773
My magic sword to defend
our land and our people

359
00:12:30,773 --> 00:12:32,913
from all manner of enemies.

360
00:12:32,913 --> 00:12:36,220
- [Servo] And get the
five bucks he owes me.

361
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:38,077
- [Voiceover] His last deed done,

362
00:12:38,077 --> 00:12:39,979
Invincor turned to stone,

363
00:12:39,979 --> 00:12:41,782
to become part of a legend

364
00:12:41,782 --> 00:12:44,211
that would live for all time.

365
00:12:44,211 --> 00:12:46,553
- [Mike] How many prologues
does this movie need?

366
00:12:46,553 --> 00:12:48,101
(Servo chuckling, dramatic music)

367
00:12:48,101 --> 00:12:51,989
- [Crow] Then they harvested
the charcoal briquettes.

368
00:12:51,989 --> 00:12:53,712
- [Servo] Oi, farmers
really need the rain, huh?

369
00:12:53,712 --> 00:12:55,490
(Mike chuckling)

370
00:12:55,490 --> 00:12:57,779
- [Crow] The heat is blowing up my skirt.

371
00:12:57,779 --> 00:12:59,206
- [Mike] Woo.

372
00:12:59,206 --> 00:13:00,656
- [Crow] Ow.

373
00:13:00,656 --> 00:13:02,223
Ow, ow, ow.

374
00:13:02,223 --> 00:13:03,316
Ow.

375
00:13:03,316 --> 00:13:06,399
- [Crow] At least I saved this stick.

376
00:13:08,850 --> 00:13:09,789
- I'm thirsty.

377
00:13:09,789 --> 00:13:10,715
- [Servo] What's your poison?

378
00:13:10,715 --> 00:13:13,031
- Patience, my son.

379
00:13:13,031 --> 00:13:14,441
- [Servo] Wow.

380
00:13:14,441 --> 00:13:15,854
I'm thirsty, I'm thirsty.

381
00:13:15,854 --> 00:13:18,414
Next I supposed you'll
want something to eat.

382
00:13:18,414 --> 00:13:21,807
I've never had anything to
drink and I've done just fine!

383
00:13:21,807 --> 00:13:25,974
- [Crow] Ah, good, they
reached the ranger station.

384
00:13:27,941 --> 00:13:30,180
- [Traveler] Good morrow
to thee, stranger.

385
00:13:30,180 --> 00:13:31,421
We are weary travelers.

386
00:13:31,421 --> 00:13:32,478
What is thy name?

387
00:13:32,478 --> 00:13:35,112
- [Stranger] I am Ilya
Murometz, son of Theodore.

388
00:13:35,112 --> 00:13:36,390
- [Servo] You pay at the first window.

389
00:13:36,390 --> 00:13:37,720
- [Traveler] Could you
bring us some water?

390
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,256
- [Ilya] Glad would I be to serve you,

391
00:13:39,256 --> 00:13:40,976
but I cannot move from this chair.

392
00:13:40,976 --> 00:13:43,221
Come into my house and drink your fill.

393
00:13:43,221 --> 00:13:44,659
- Thank you!

394
00:13:44,659 --> 00:13:45,492
Come.

395
00:13:45,492 --> 00:13:48,039
- [Crow] I should warn
you, I'm just a torso.

396
00:13:48,039 --> 00:13:51,017
- [Servo] Jellystone Park.

397
00:13:51,017 --> 00:13:52,870
- [Mike] He's got a poster of Sun Ra.

398
00:13:52,870 --> 00:13:55,102
(Servo chuckling)

399
00:13:55,102 --> 00:13:56,670
- Greetings to thee, Ilya.

400
00:13:56,670 --> 00:13:57,503
- [Crow] Yeah, yeah.

401
00:13:57,503 --> 00:13:58,746
Could you bring me a magazine?

402
00:13:58,746 --> 00:14:00,019
- I know you gentle pilgrims

403
00:14:00,019 --> 00:14:01,536
have traveled far and wide.

404
00:14:01,536 --> 00:14:02,636
- [Servo] Member, FDIC.

405
00:14:02,636 --> 00:14:03,674
- Tell me of the evils

406
00:14:03,674 --> 00:14:05,136
that have befallen our troubled country

407
00:14:05,136 --> 00:14:06,539
in these days of darkness.

408
00:14:06,539 --> 00:14:08,302
- Our poor and troubled land

409
00:14:08,302 --> 00:14:10,680
is plunged into woe deep as the sea.

410
00:14:10,680 --> 00:14:13,540
Those cursed Tougars
plunder, rob, and kill.

411
00:14:13,540 --> 00:14:16,954
- If only I had my strength back.

412
00:14:16,954 --> 00:14:20,504
I could help defend my
country in her hour of need.

413
00:14:20,504 --> 00:14:23,671
- [Crow] But I've been classified 4-F.

414
00:14:24,781 --> 00:14:27,119
I could beat this guy up!

415
00:14:27,119 --> 00:14:28,956
- Drink the dew of the magic grass, Ilya,

416
00:14:28,956 --> 00:14:31,182
and perhaps thy strength will return.

417
00:14:31,182 --> 00:14:32,399
- [Mike] Here's some Haley's M-O.

418
00:14:32,399 --> 00:14:33,783
- Thank you, my son.

419
00:14:33,783 --> 00:14:37,270
- [Traveler] Drink this, young man.

420
00:14:37,270 --> 00:14:39,103
Drink hearty and pray.

421
00:14:40,374 --> 00:14:43,791
- [Servo] Please, sir, could I have more?

422
00:14:44,911 --> 00:14:47,234
- [Crow] Ilya likes carrots, doesn't he?

423
00:14:47,234 --> 00:14:48,377
- Dost thou feel

424
00:14:48,377 --> 00:14:50,405
the strength returning
to thy veins yet, Ilya?

425
00:14:50,405 --> 00:14:51,725
- [Crow] I'm less thirsty.

426
00:14:51,725 --> 00:14:52,992
- Yes, yes, I can.

427
00:14:52,992 --> 00:14:54,211
- [Servo] Coppin' a buzz.

428
00:14:54,211 --> 00:14:55,044
- But.

429
00:14:55,044 --> 00:14:57,175
- [Servo] The walls are moving.

430
00:14:57,175 --> 00:15:00,205
(Ilya groaning)

431
00:15:00,205 --> 00:15:02,069
- I still cannot move.

432
00:15:02,069 --> 00:15:03,559
- Patience, my Ilya.

433
00:15:03,559 --> 00:15:08,444
Thy strength shall indeed
return, I promise thee.

434
00:15:08,444 --> 00:15:10,773
- [Mike] Uh, hold on,
I'm havin' a montage.

435
00:15:10,773 --> 00:15:13,452
- [Crow] It's the line for Wild Mountain!

436
00:15:13,452 --> 00:15:16,202
(dramatic music)

437
00:15:20,658 --> 00:15:22,514
- [Servo] Oh, that was one high colonic.

438
00:15:22,514 --> 00:15:25,181
Yes, sir, I feel like a new man!

439
00:15:29,410 --> 00:15:33,824
- [Crow] Let's get you back
to your room, Mr. Torkelson.

440
00:15:33,824 --> 00:15:34,714
- [Mike] I'll take these.

441
00:15:34,714 --> 00:15:37,186
I'll just wear them outta the store.

442
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,701
- [Servo] I feel good all under.

443
00:15:38,701 --> 00:15:39,534
First thing, I take off the burlap dress.

444
00:15:39,534 --> 00:15:42,367
(uplifting music)

445
00:15:45,714 --> 00:15:48,666
- [Mike] And now, ladies and gentlemen,

446
00:15:48,666 --> 00:15:50,088
the Swedish Moses of soul!

447
00:15:50,088 --> 00:15:52,467
- [Servo] Aw, hey, who left all my tools

448
00:15:52,467 --> 00:15:54,374
laying around in the front yard?

449
00:15:54,374 --> 00:15:57,207
- [Mike] I'm feeling
positively demonstrative.

450
00:15:57,207 --> 00:16:00,457
I could almost tell my wife I love her!

451
00:16:01,996 --> 00:16:03,880
- [Crow] Oh, I need to
sit down for a while,

452
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:05,825
believe it or not.

453
00:16:05,825 --> 00:16:07,592
- Take thou the magic sword of Invincor,

454
00:16:07,592 --> 00:16:08,725
and be though like them.

455
00:16:08,725 --> 00:16:11,536
- [Servo] We don't wanna carry it anymore.

456
00:16:11,536 --> 00:16:14,286
(dramatic music)

457
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,941
This is the best-tasting sword ever!

458
00:16:17,941 --> 00:16:19,300
- Thank you, good friends.

459
00:16:19,300 --> 00:16:22,300
(MST3K theme music)

460
00:16:25,810 --> 00:16:30,023
I sold the sword and
bought some Finnish vodka.

461
00:16:30,023 --> 00:16:31,951
- [Mike] Yep, pretty much.

462
00:16:31,951 --> 00:16:34,484
- Ah, how my hands yearn to
feel the good, rich earth,

463
00:16:34,484 --> 00:16:36,812
and the honest toil of
the farmer once again.

464
00:16:36,812 --> 00:16:38,609
- [Crow] Go ahead and grab a plow then!

465
00:16:38,609 --> 00:16:40,678
- [Ilya] Work the fields of with father.

466
00:16:40,678 --> 00:16:43,322
- [Servo] I thought he was the father.

467
00:16:43,322 --> 00:16:45,036
- [Mike] It's a good crop of stumps.

468
00:16:45,036 --> 00:16:46,356
(Servo chuckling)

469
00:16:46,356 --> 00:16:47,507
(crashing)

470
00:16:47,507 --> 00:16:49,633
- [Crow] Da, hold on, I'll get the Bobcat.

471
00:16:49,633 --> 00:16:50,800
- [Servo] Wow.

472
00:16:51,908 --> 00:16:53,811
Uh, we want that.

473
00:16:53,811 --> 00:16:55,432
- [Ilya] Root up the tree stumps.

474
00:16:55,432 --> 00:16:59,891
- [Mike] ♫ And we'll have
a tree stump of fun ♫

475
00:16:59,891 --> 00:17:02,401
(Ilya grunting, mumbling)

476
00:17:02,401 --> 00:17:05,427
- [Crow] I'll see how many
times I can skip this!

477
00:17:05,427 --> 00:17:06,444
(crashing)

478
00:17:06,444 --> 00:17:07,520
- [Servo] Sure, go ahead,

479
00:17:07,520 --> 00:17:09,221
use the fjord for your garbage dump, Ilya.

480
00:17:09,221 --> 00:17:10,127
- Hard as stone,

481
00:17:10,127 --> 00:17:12,178
thou has been no earth of my father's.

482
00:17:12,178 --> 00:17:13,138
- [Mike] Grandpa, no.

483
00:17:13,138 --> 00:17:16,504
- Soft as the down of the
swan will though become.

484
00:17:16,504 --> 00:17:18,842
- The mighty falcon lifts his wings

485
00:17:18,842 --> 00:17:20,284
and is ready to fly again.

486
00:17:20,284 --> 00:17:21,902
- Our son is like a man reborn.

487
00:17:21,902 --> 00:17:24,336
- With strong hands, shall
help work our fields.

488
00:17:24,336 --> 00:17:26,096
- [Crow] The banjo
becomes angry at midnight.

489
00:17:26,096 --> 00:17:27,701
What the hell are you talking about!

490
00:17:27,701 --> 00:17:29,135
- Forgive me, dear mother.

491
00:17:29,135 --> 00:17:30,187
- [Servo] I overreacted.

492
00:17:30,187 --> 00:17:31,669
- But I cannot till the land.

493
00:17:31,669 --> 00:17:33,972
Or reap its riches.

494
00:17:33,972 --> 00:17:36,206
Kalin and his plunderers
aim their deadly arrows

495
00:17:36,206 --> 00:17:38,627
at the heart of our country
at this very moment.

496
00:17:38,627 --> 00:17:39,460
- [Mike] Oh, well.

497
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:41,632
- I cannot remain here
while our country suffers.

498
00:17:41,632 --> 00:17:44,183
- [Crow] So you're coppin' out again!

499
00:17:44,183 --> 00:17:46,226
- [Ilya] Give me your
blessing, dear parents.

500
00:17:46,226 --> 00:17:47,338
- [Crow] You want the car, don'tcha?

501
00:17:47,338 --> 00:17:48,674
- [Ilya] Now I must go forth.

502
00:17:48,674 --> 00:17:51,427
- What you tell us lies
heavy on my heart, my son.

503
00:17:51,427 --> 00:17:53,557
- [Ilya] I go because I must, Mother.

504
00:17:53,557 --> 00:17:54,838
My country needs me.

505
00:17:54,838 --> 00:17:57,414
- I give you my blessing, Ilya, my son.

506
00:17:57,414 --> 00:17:58,351
Go in peace.

507
00:17:58,351 --> 00:18:00,637
- [Mike] Why are you older than me, son?

508
00:18:00,637 --> 00:18:02,659
- Guard against evil, my son.

509
00:18:02,659 --> 00:18:04,703
And help your fellow man.

510
00:18:04,703 --> 00:18:05,855
- [Servo] But not Murray.

511
00:18:05,855 --> 00:18:09,995
- [Ilya] I shall remember
your wishes always, Mother.

512
00:18:09,995 --> 00:18:11,638
- [Crow] Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey!

513
00:18:11,638 --> 00:18:13,388
You're in the wrong myth!

514
00:18:13,388 --> 00:18:15,054
- You will need a strong horse.

515
00:18:15,054 --> 00:18:17,124
I would like to give you mine, Ilya.

516
00:18:17,124 --> 00:18:19,090
His name is Chestnut Gray.

517
00:18:19,090 --> 00:18:21,119
- [Mike] Oh, that's okay, I'll walk.

518
00:18:21,119 --> 00:18:22,346
(horse neighing)

519
00:18:22,346 --> 00:18:25,547
- Do not concern yourself
over his small size.

520
00:18:25,547 --> 00:18:27,284
Bathe him three times in dew,

521
00:18:27,284 --> 00:18:29,619
and he will grow until he becomes

522
00:18:29,619 --> 00:18:32,928
the mightiest of all the
steeds you have ever known.

523
00:18:32,928 --> 00:18:34,938
- [Servo] Jeez, I'm running late as it is.

524
00:18:34,938 --> 00:18:36,385
(serene music)

525
00:18:36,385 --> 00:18:37,707
- [Crow] Well, let's
get you far enough away

526
00:18:37,707 --> 00:18:39,563
where they won't hear the gunshot.

527
00:18:39,563 --> 00:18:40,410
- [Mike] No!

528
00:18:40,410 --> 00:18:42,827
- [Ilya] Grow, Chestnut Gray.

529
00:18:43,730 --> 00:18:44,563
Grow.

530
00:18:44,563 --> 00:18:45,591
- [Crow] Isn't he supposed to

531
00:18:45,591 --> 00:18:47,686
bathe him in Mountain Dew or (mumbles).

532
00:18:47,686 --> 00:18:49,588
- [Ilya] Be thou as fleet
of foot as the deer.

533
00:18:49,588 --> 00:18:52,660
- [Servo] Buy bonds
where you work or bank.

534
00:18:52,660 --> 00:18:56,327
- [Ilya] Swim rivers
faster than the salmon.

535
00:18:57,839 --> 00:19:00,385
Streak across the ground
swifter than the wolf,

536
00:19:00,385 --> 00:19:03,932
higher than the falcon
winging through the sky.

537
00:19:03,932 --> 00:19:06,866
- [Mike] Longer than there've
been fishes in the ocean.

538
00:19:06,866 --> 00:19:07,699
- [Servo] Hmm?

539
00:19:07,699 --> 00:19:10,183
- [Ilya] When a stranger
calls, hear him not.

540
00:19:10,183 --> 00:19:11,016
But when you hear my voice.

541
00:19:11,016 --> 00:19:12,183
- [Servo] Run!

542
00:19:13,790 --> 00:19:16,598
- Come swiftly like the wind.

543
00:19:16,598 --> 00:19:18,015
- [Crow] Anything else, your highness?

544
00:19:18,015 --> 00:19:19,886
- [Ilya] We shall be friends unto death.

545
00:19:19,886 --> 00:19:21,755
In deed and in battle.

546
00:19:21,755 --> 00:19:23,497
- [Mike] Oh-ho, I don't do battle.

547
00:19:23,497 --> 00:19:24,862
- [Ilya] Good Chestnut Gray.

548
00:19:24,862 --> 00:19:27,679
- [Servo] Look, I got an
offer from Calumet Farms.

549
00:19:27,679 --> 00:19:30,132
- [Ilya] Serve me well, noble steed.

550
00:19:30,132 --> 00:19:33,734
- [Mike] He is a lonely, lonely man.

551
00:19:33,734 --> 00:19:37,783
- [Crow] Connery. Snipes.
(serene music)

552
00:19:37,783 --> 00:19:41,025
- [Servo] Daily affirmations.

553
00:19:41,025 --> 00:19:45,331
- [Mike] The Duluth Chamber
of Commerce bids you adieu.

554
00:19:45,331 --> 00:19:47,648
- [Crow] And wherever Ilya went,

555
00:19:47,648 --> 00:19:49,365
he carried his pool cue.

556
00:19:49,365 --> 00:19:50,875
- [Servo] Aw, Jeez.

557
00:19:50,875 --> 00:19:53,292
Cast it right into the weeds.

558
00:19:54,516 --> 00:19:56,381
(Mike sniffling)

559
00:19:56,381 --> 00:19:57,843
- [Servo] Nevermore!
(crow cawing)

560
00:19:57,843 --> 00:19:59,879
- [Voiceover] Follow the right road,

561
00:19:59,879 --> 00:20:01,704
and you will find riches!

562
00:20:01,704 --> 00:20:04,237
- [Voiceover] Follow the left road,

563
00:20:04,237 --> 00:20:06,320
and you will find a wife.

564
00:20:07,708 --> 00:20:10,189
- [Voiceover] Go straight ahead,

565
00:20:10,189 --> 00:20:11,972
and you will find death.

566
00:20:11,972 --> 00:20:14,217
- [Crow] Chestnut Gray,
quit doin' your impressions.

567
00:20:14,217 --> 00:20:16,539
- [Ilya] Riches would give me little joy.

568
00:20:16,539 --> 00:20:17,605
- [Servo] But I'll take 'em anyway.

569
00:20:17,605 --> 00:20:19,473
- [Ilya] Now is not time to woo me a wife.

570
00:20:19,473 --> 00:20:20,702
- [Servo] But I'll take one anyway.

571
00:20:20,702 --> 00:20:23,859
- [Ilya] So, I shall follow
the road that leads to death.

572
00:20:23,859 --> 00:20:26,141
- [Crow] I might not get to death tonight.

573
00:20:26,141 --> 00:20:28,349
I may spend the night at serious injury,

574
00:20:28,349 --> 00:20:33,106
and head over to permanent
disability in the mornin'.

575
00:20:33,106 --> 00:20:35,713
- [Mike] ♫ No, I don't wanna fall ♫

576
00:20:35,713 --> 00:20:38,000
(Mike mumbling)

577
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:41,399
- [Servo] Chen, round up
every Finn on the island.

578
00:20:41,399 --> 00:20:44,232
(Servo chuckling)

579
00:20:45,346 --> 00:20:47,547
- [Crow] Thou shalt seek shelter

580
00:20:47,547 --> 00:20:50,474
in the southwest corner of thy basement.

581
00:20:50,474 --> 00:20:52,823
(crow cawing)

582
00:20:52,823 --> 00:20:55,761
- [Mike] Where are the ROUSs?

583
00:20:55,761 --> 00:20:58,491
- [Crow] Oh, this is downtown death.

584
00:20:58,491 --> 00:21:00,912
(crow cawing)

585
00:21:00,912 --> 00:21:02,412
- [Servo] Woo-woo!

586
00:21:05,529 --> 00:21:08,379
- [Crow] This movie has a
real View-Master quality.

587
00:21:08,379 --> 00:21:10,211
(Servo emulating movie's sound effects)

588
00:21:10,211 --> 00:21:11,848
- [Mike] Uh, why did
Invincor like this job?

589
00:21:11,848 --> 00:21:14,598
(horse neighing)

590
00:21:17,727 --> 00:21:20,612
- Go straight ahead and
you will find death!

591
00:21:20,612 --> 00:21:21,588
- [Servo] Aagh!
- [Crow] Ooh.

592
00:21:21,588 --> 00:21:22,421
- [Mike] Euw.

593
00:21:22,421 --> 00:21:24,694
Maybe he has a good personality.

594
00:21:24,694 --> 00:21:25,947
(shrill sound effect, wind whirring)

595
00:21:25,947 --> 00:21:28,169
- [Crow] Whoa, blech, Dorito breath.

596
00:21:28,169 --> 00:21:30,489
(foreboding music)

597
00:21:30,489 --> 00:21:33,754
- [Servo] Dizzy Gillespie-esque.

598
00:21:33,754 --> 00:21:34,889
- [Mike] Oh, that's always nice.

599
00:21:34,889 --> 00:21:37,072
Just blow the leaves
into the neighbors' yard.

600
00:21:37,072 --> 00:21:40,572
- [Crow] Couldn't the wind just cry, Mary?

601
00:21:41,712 --> 00:21:46,307
(wind whirring, branches snapping)

602
00:21:46,307 --> 00:21:47,962
- Do not fear this wind demon!

603
00:21:47,962 --> 00:21:48,872
- [Crow] You know, sometimes I wake up,

604
00:21:48,872 --> 00:21:50,311
and I feel like this guy looks.

605
00:21:50,311 --> 00:21:51,478
- [Servo] Ooh.

606
00:21:52,702 --> 00:21:56,625
- [Ilya] It cannot harm
you, Chestnut Gray!

607
00:21:56,625 --> 00:21:59,516
- [Servo] Yeah, sure, let's
go down the road to death.

608
00:21:59,516 --> 00:22:00,349
Fine.

609
00:22:00,349 --> 00:22:01,653
What the hell was I thinkin'?

610
00:22:01,653 --> 00:22:02,642
(shrill sound effect, wind whirring)

611
00:22:02,642 --> 00:22:06,527
- [Mike] Chesnut Gray is like
the Chevy Suburban of horses.

612
00:22:06,527 --> 00:22:07,390
(crashing)

613
00:22:07,390 --> 00:22:08,622
(Crow laughing)

614
00:22:08,622 --> 00:22:09,612
- [Servo] Oh, sure, yeah.

615
00:22:09,612 --> 00:22:10,445
Lucky shot.

616
00:22:10,445 --> 00:22:13,195
(exciting music)

617
00:22:13,195 --> 00:22:15,991
- [Servo] I can explain everything, heh.

618
00:22:15,991 --> 00:22:17,641
- Looks like a fat owl, this one,

619
00:22:17,641 --> 00:22:19,613
and yet he cries rivers of tears.

620
00:22:19,613 --> 00:22:20,580
- [Crow] I'm a wind demon.

621
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:21,413
It's my job!

622
00:22:21,413 --> 00:22:22,504
- I shall take you to my prince,

623
00:22:22,504 --> 00:22:24,673
and he will decide what to do with you.

624
00:22:24,673 --> 00:22:28,054
- [Mike] Okay, let me put on my good fur.

625
00:22:28,054 --> 00:22:29,538
- [Prince] Princes, nobles, and warriors,

626
00:22:29,538 --> 00:22:31,231
here I sit with you in judgment,

627
00:22:31,231 --> 00:22:33,391
and here with you do I hold court.

628
00:22:33,391 --> 00:22:34,589
If there be any wrongdoers,

629
00:22:34,589 --> 00:22:37,086
let them be brought
before us for judgment.

630
00:22:37,086 --> 00:22:39,503
- [Crow] Bring up Al D'Amato.

631
00:22:41,752 --> 00:22:44,919
- [Servo] I like having court outside.

632
00:22:46,143 --> 00:22:47,940
- This villain must be
punished, good prince.

633
00:22:47,940 --> 00:22:49,829
He tore my mare's tail off!

634
00:22:49,829 --> 00:22:51,641
You must find a suitable punishment,

635
00:22:51,641 --> 00:22:53,380
for what he has done is a bad thing!

636
00:22:53,380 --> 00:22:54,306
- It is bad.

637
00:22:54,306 --> 00:22:57,067
- He has also stolen the royal timber!

638
00:22:57,067 --> 00:22:58,268
- He must be a villain.

639
00:22:58,268 --> 00:22:59,208
- Yes, sire.

640
00:22:59,208 --> 00:23:00,650
- [Servo] Kris Kristofferson!

641
00:23:00,650 --> 00:23:02,389
- It is true that I did this things.

642
00:23:02,389 --> 00:23:04,358
But I had a very good reason, sire.

643
00:23:04,358 --> 00:23:06,374
He loaned me his horse, but not harness,

644
00:23:06,374 --> 00:23:08,572
so I tied the wagon to the horse's tail.

645
00:23:08,572 --> 00:23:09,405
(crowd laughing)

646
00:23:09,405 --> 00:23:10,726
That's how it happened, sire.

647
00:23:10,726 --> 00:23:12,758
- [Crow] It's the Finnish
version of Night Court!

648
00:23:12,758 --> 00:23:13,998
- He should be sent to prison!

649
00:23:13,998 --> 00:23:16,151
He must be punished!

650
00:23:16,151 --> 00:23:17,766
- This is our verdict.

651
00:23:17,766 --> 00:23:18,949
- [Mike] I'll allow the DNA.

652
00:23:18,949 --> 00:23:20,230
- You, Vargarren.

653
00:23:20,230 --> 00:23:23,079
Give him your horse to
ride through the forest

654
00:23:23,079 --> 00:23:26,053
until her tail shall grow back again.

655
00:23:26,053 --> 00:23:27,905
This is our judgment.

656
00:23:27,905 --> 00:23:29,830
- [Vargarren] Justice,
Regent Prince, justice!!

657
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:31,083
- [Crow] Get up, you brown-noser.

658
00:23:31,083 --> 00:23:31,916
- And remember, young man,

659
00:23:31,916 --> 00:23:34,343
you must return the horse to
Vargarren in good condition.

660
00:23:34,343 --> 00:23:35,176
- [Crow] And enter drug rehab.

661
00:23:35,176 --> 00:23:36,444
- Yes, sire.

662
00:23:36,444 --> 00:23:38,127
I swear it.

663
00:23:38,127 --> 00:23:39,228
- [Mike] It's kingdom of Robert Borks.

664
00:23:39,228 --> 00:23:40,588
- [Man] Radiant Prince!

665
00:23:40,588 --> 00:23:42,726
Durbar, the mighty warrior,

666
00:23:42,726 --> 00:23:43,891
has returned to the palace!

667
00:23:43,891 --> 00:23:45,791
- [Servo] Uh, he's the artist

668
00:23:45,791 --> 00:23:46,624
formerly known as Radiant Prince.

669
00:23:46,624 --> 00:23:48,420
- Summon all the nobles for a great feast.

670
00:23:48,420 --> 00:23:50,888
And see that all these
people are fed well.

671
00:23:50,888 --> 00:23:51,749
(crowd cheering)

672
00:23:51,749 --> 00:23:52,582
- [Servo] I need a veggie meal!

673
00:23:52,582 --> 00:23:53,469
- [Mike] Can I bring my cousin?

674
00:23:53,469 --> 00:23:54,732
- [Crow] I'm lactose intolerant.

675
00:23:54,732 --> 00:23:56,726
- [Servo] Can I have the money instead?

676
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:57,801
- [Crow] But I don't like food.

677
00:23:57,801 --> 00:23:59,533
- The noble prince invites you all

678
00:23:59,533 --> 00:24:01,022
to the feast at the palace!

679
00:24:01,022 --> 00:24:04,522
(metal clanging, beeping)

680
00:24:17,305 --> 00:24:19,972
(clock ticking)

681
00:24:41,859 --> 00:24:45,776
- Once, on the shore of
The Great Northern Sea,

682
00:24:46,937 --> 00:24:49,437
two men stood alone on a pier.

683
00:24:59,080 --> 00:25:03,567
(water rushing, wind whirring)

684
00:25:03,567 --> 00:25:04,400
- Sven?

685
00:25:09,921 --> 00:25:13,838
(water rushing, wind whirring)

686
00:25:26,290 --> 00:25:27,290
- Yah, Olie?

687
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:38,237
(water rushing, wind whirring)

688
00:25:39,966 --> 00:25:42,966
(foghorn bellowing)

689
00:25:49,534 --> 00:25:52,117
- There came into me a thought.

690
00:25:59,131 --> 00:26:03,214
(water rushing, gulls squawking)

691
00:26:16,149 --> 00:26:16,982
- Yah?

692
00:26:23,258 --> 00:26:27,008
(water rushing, dog barking)

693
00:26:41,050 --> 00:26:44,300
- I will count the boards of this pier.

694
00:26:50,164 --> 00:26:54,081
(water rushing, wind whirring)

695
00:26:56,562 --> 00:26:57,395
- Yah?

696
00:26:58,601 --> 00:26:59,434
- And you.

697
00:27:02,856 --> 00:27:03,689
- Yah?

698
00:27:06,308 --> 00:27:09,773
(water rushing)

699
00:27:09,773 --> 00:27:13,606
- You will count the
slits between the boards.

700
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:20,741
(water rushing)

701
00:27:20,741 --> 00:27:22,158
- You, da boards.

702
00:27:23,322 --> 00:27:24,155
And, I,

703
00:27:26,501 --> 00:27:27,334
da slits.

704
00:27:30,611 --> 00:27:31,444
- Yah.

705
00:27:36,067 --> 00:27:40,150
(water rushing, gulls squawking)

706
00:27:41,988 --> 00:27:44,388
- (gasping) Begin.

707
00:27:44,388 --> 00:27:46,930
(water rushing, wind whirring)

708
00:27:46,930 --> 00:27:47,763
- One.

709
00:27:47,763 --> 00:27:48,692
- One.

710
00:27:48,692 --> 00:27:49,525
- Two.

711
00:27:51,263 --> 00:27:52,096
- Two.

712
00:27:54,399 --> 00:27:55,232
- Tree.

713
00:27:56,306 --> 00:27:57,139
- Tree.

714
00:27:59,149 --> 00:27:59,982
- Four.

715
00:28:01,798 --> 00:28:02,631
- Four.

716
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:04,653
- Five.

717
00:28:06,322 --> 00:28:07,155
- Five.

718
00:28:09,148 --> 00:28:09,981
- Six.

719
00:28:10,973 --> 00:28:12,140
- Six. Aaaagh!

720
00:28:15,268 --> 00:28:17,601
(splashing)

721
00:28:18,508 --> 00:28:20,091
- And so you see...

722
00:28:21,612 --> 00:28:23,695
When you're out of slits,

723
00:28:26,550 --> 00:28:28,133
you're out of pier.

724
00:28:32,394 --> 00:28:36,144
(water rushing, dog barking)

725
00:28:41,027 --> 00:28:43,694
(crowd singing)

726
00:28:47,176 --> 00:28:49,751
- [Crow] It may be the wine,
Lars, but you're a pretty men.

727
00:28:49,751 --> 00:28:50,922
- [Servo] Sven, no, don't.

728
00:28:50,922 --> 00:28:51,922
You mustn't.

729
00:28:53,458 --> 00:28:56,281
- [Mike] Who's the new guy?

730
00:28:56,281 --> 00:28:58,647
- [Servo] We'll be showing
the Vikes-Packers game

731
00:28:58,647 --> 00:29:00,206
in just a few minutes, everyone.

732
00:29:00,206 --> 00:29:01,731
- [Ilya] Excuse me, good people.

733
00:29:01,731 --> 00:29:03,653
- [Servo] Where's the men's room?

734
00:29:03,653 --> 00:29:05,477
- [Ilya] Which among you is Prince Vanda?

735
00:29:05,477 --> 00:29:07,506
- Why do you ask for the prince?

736
00:29:07,506 --> 00:29:09,144
A bumpkin like you belongs there,

737
00:29:09,144 --> 00:29:11,501
at the foot of the
table with the peasants.

738
00:29:11,501 --> 00:29:13,362
- [Feast Guest] You are too
harsh with this stranger, Alexi.

739
00:29:13,362 --> 00:29:14,575
Let him be heard.

740
00:29:14,575 --> 00:29:16,453
Perhaps he brings important news.

741
00:29:16,453 --> 00:29:18,976
- [Crow] Yeah, like where
the best buffets are.

742
00:29:18,976 --> 00:29:21,105
- [Ilya] I came here not
to feast, good nobles,

743
00:29:21,105 --> 00:29:24,003
but to serve my prince and my country.

744
00:29:24,003 --> 00:29:25,175
- And I say you're not fit

745
00:29:25,175 --> 00:29:26,726
to sit at the same table with a noble!

746
00:29:26,726 --> 00:29:28,978
- [Servo] Nah-nah-nah-nah-nah-nah.

747
00:29:28,978 --> 00:29:29,820
- You a noble?

748
00:29:29,820 --> 00:29:32,392
More likely you joust with
milkmaids behind the barn.

749
00:29:32,392 --> 00:29:33,808
(feast guests laughing)

750
00:29:33,808 --> 00:29:35,138
- [Crow] I'm not gay!

751
00:29:35,138 --> 00:29:36,179
(feast guests laughing)

752
00:29:36,179 --> 00:29:38,597
He's the Finnish Oscar Wilde.

753
00:29:38,597 --> 00:29:40,361
- Make way for the noble Mekhai,

754
00:29:40,361 --> 00:29:42,569
bearing rare and costly
gifts for our prince.

755
00:29:42,569 --> 00:29:44,726
- Good health and
greetings, Radiant Prince.

756
00:29:44,726 --> 00:29:47,782
- [Mike] Look, I don't
book openers anymore.

757
00:29:47,782 --> 00:29:49,624
- I have collected all taxes and tributes.

758
00:29:49,624 --> 00:29:51,466
I was sorely wounded in battle,

759
00:29:51,466 --> 00:29:53,214
but I rounded them all.

760
00:29:53,214 --> 00:29:55,227
All your enemies!

761
00:29:55,227 --> 00:29:57,516
- [Servo] Anyways, here's
some o'the stuff we got.

762
00:29:57,516 --> 00:29:59,717
- Dear prince, for you
alone, I would do it again.

763
00:29:59,717 --> 00:30:01,107
I would gladly lay down my life--

764
00:30:01,107 --> 00:30:02,291
- [Crow] For a hamburger today.

765
00:30:02,291 --> 00:30:04,448
- Prince, I bested the mighty Sartag,

766
00:30:04,448 --> 00:30:07,259
for you I would gladly give my life.

767
00:30:07,259 --> 00:30:08,092
- [Mike] No.

768
00:30:08,092 --> 00:30:08,925
No lick!

769
00:30:08,925 --> 00:30:11,275
- So say we all, every one of us.

770
00:30:11,275 --> 00:30:12,700
- The wind demon attacked me,

771
00:30:12,700 --> 00:30:15,098
and I cut him to ribbons
in the enchanted forest.

772
00:30:15,098 --> 00:30:16,246
- He lies, my prince.

773
00:30:16,246 --> 00:30:18,193
- [Servo] I saw him wet
them on the field of honor.

774
00:30:18,193 --> 00:30:21,142
- I know that he has not even
set eyes on the wind demon.

775
00:30:21,142 --> 00:30:23,062
- [Prince] Who are you, good stranger?

776
00:30:23,062 --> 00:30:24,896
And where do you come from?

777
00:30:24,896 --> 00:30:26,717
- I am Ilya Murometz.

778
00:30:26,717 --> 00:30:28,493
I am from Muldova.

779
00:30:28,493 --> 00:30:31,029
My father has a small
farm there near the river.

780
00:30:31,029 --> 00:30:32,545
- [Crow] Oh, oops, dropped a cuff link.

781
00:30:32,545 --> 00:30:34,767
- And have you yourself
seen the wind demon?

782
00:30:34,767 --> 00:30:37,476
- I will show him to you.

783
00:30:37,476 --> 00:30:38,794
- [Servo] Say hello to the nice people,

784
00:30:38,794 --> 00:30:40,563
wind demon.
- [Ilya] Here is the evil one.

785
00:30:40,563 --> 00:30:42,320
Not very big, but he's
as mean as he looks.

786
00:30:42,320 --> 00:30:44,083
- [Prince] I've never seen such a monster.

787
00:30:44,083 --> 00:30:46,060
Command him to whistle as loud as he can.

788
00:30:46,060 --> 00:30:47,836
- [Princess] Can he
really create the wind?

789
00:30:47,836 --> 00:30:48,673
- [Ilya] That he can do.

790
00:30:48,673 --> 00:30:50,225
But do not let him frighten you.

791
00:30:50,225 --> 00:30:51,701
- [Crow] Do you eat lunch?

792
00:30:51,701 --> 00:30:52,801
- Wait, Alicia.

793
00:30:52,801 --> 00:30:54,703
Please, do not run away.

794
00:30:54,703 --> 00:30:55,800
- [Mike] Wang Chung with me.

795
00:30:55,800 --> 00:30:58,016
- Someone will see us here.

796
00:30:58,016 --> 00:31:00,379
- I do not care, as
long as we're together.

797
00:31:00,379 --> 00:31:03,145
- My brothers say I'm too
young to be wooed, Alexi.

798
00:31:03,145 --> 00:31:05,504
- I cannot live without you.
- [Crow] Statutory woo.

799
00:31:05,504 --> 00:31:07,565
- You belong to me, Alicia.

800
00:31:07,565 --> 00:31:08,693
(gasping, swooning)

801
00:31:08,693 --> 00:31:10,287
- [Servo] Oh, Captain Spaulding!

802
00:31:10,287 --> 00:31:12,402
- Now whistle, you ugly wind demon,

803
00:31:12,402 --> 00:31:14,912
but only with half of your strength.

804
00:31:14,912 --> 00:31:16,641
- [Mike] Clint Howard!

805
00:31:16,641 --> 00:31:19,413
(Servo grunting and sputtering)

806
00:31:19,413 --> 00:31:21,913
- Now whistle, even one, hmmm?

807
00:31:23,333 --> 00:31:26,224
- [Servo] You know how
to whistle, don't you?

808
00:31:26,224 --> 00:31:28,114
(inhaling, shrill sound
effect, wind whirring)

809
00:31:28,114 --> 00:31:28,947
- [Crow] Oh, yuck!

810
00:31:28,947 --> 00:31:30,759
He was eating crackers!

811
00:31:30,759 --> 00:31:33,716
- [Servo] ♫ The summer wind demon

812
00:31:33,716 --> 00:31:36,343
♫ Came blowin' in

813
00:31:36,343 --> 00:31:39,009
♫ Roll up the barrells ♫

814
00:31:39,009 --> 00:31:39,942
(all three laughing)

815
00:31:39,942 --> 00:31:44,109
- [Crow] Clean up's a
breeze, thanks to wind demon!

816
00:31:45,992 --> 00:31:47,304
- Alicia!

817
00:31:47,304 --> 00:31:49,403
- [Mike] Wacky sight gaga
of ancient Finlandia.

818
00:31:49,403 --> 00:31:50,623
(woman shuddering)

819
00:31:50,623 --> 00:31:52,983
- [Servo] Mrs. Brittenhouse!

820
00:31:52,983 --> 00:31:55,493
- [Crow] Man, I'm killin' tonight!

821
00:31:55,493 --> 00:31:58,494
- [Mike] The wind hooked me to a cable!

822
00:31:58,494 --> 00:32:02,485
- [Servo] ♫ Everyone knows it's windy ♫

823
00:32:02,485 --> 00:32:03,485
- [Crow] Oh.

824
00:32:05,294 --> 00:32:07,125
- [Mike] The wind demon
has killed a lotta people,

825
00:32:07,125 --> 00:32:08,311
but it's all in good fun.

826
00:32:08,311 --> 00:32:09,807
(all three chuckling)

827
00:32:09,807 --> 00:32:11,664
- Stop him, Ilya, make him stop!

828
00:32:11,664 --> 00:32:13,730
- Stop him before he blows us away.

829
00:32:13,730 --> 00:32:15,010
- Stop, we've seen enough.

830
00:32:15,010 --> 00:32:16,111
Make him stop.

831
00:32:16,111 --> 00:32:18,004
- Hold your breath, spawn of the devil.

832
00:32:18,004 --> 00:32:20,104
You have performed your last evil deed.

833
00:32:20,104 --> 00:32:21,680
- [Crow] Hey, you asked me!

834
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:23,932
- No more chill them
with your blasts of wind.

835
00:32:23,932 --> 00:32:25,106
- This country bumpkin is

836
00:32:25,106 --> 00:32:26,362
quite a fellow, I say.
- [Mike] Yes.

837
00:32:26,362 --> 00:32:28,029
Jolly good, old man.

838
00:32:30,751 --> 00:32:33,335
- [Crow] Oh, yuck, he's in the spittoon.

839
00:32:33,335 --> 00:32:34,678
- [Mike] That was pretty good.

840
00:32:34,678 --> 00:32:35,678
Can he scat?

841
00:32:37,080 --> 00:32:38,276
- [Prince] Take this, Ilya,

842
00:32:38,276 --> 00:32:41,217
as a reward for your service.

843
00:32:41,217 --> 00:32:44,674
As for this demon, his
reward will match his deeds.

844
00:32:44,674 --> 00:32:47,011
- [Servo] Put him in my private chambers.

845
00:32:47,011 --> 00:32:49,069
(demon hissing)

846
00:32:49,069 --> 00:32:51,327
- [Crow] I gotta blow, ha-ha-ha!

847
00:32:51,327 --> 00:32:54,332
- [Alexi] You are a man
after my own heart, Ilya.

848
00:32:54,332 --> 00:32:57,256
- [Mike] Wanna start a band?

849
00:32:57,256 --> 00:32:59,689
- [Servo] And so, ZZ Top was born.

850
00:32:59,689 --> 00:33:01,020
- Take no offense of Alexi.

851
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:02,478
He has a quick temper,

852
00:33:02,478 --> 00:33:04,066
but he is a brave and courageous soldier.

853
00:33:04,066 --> 00:33:04,899
Let us be friends.

854
00:33:04,899 --> 00:33:07,067
- [Crow] I'm Bob from marketing.

855
00:33:07,067 --> 00:33:09,286
(triumphant music)

856
00:33:09,286 --> 00:33:10,345
- [Ilya] We shall be friends.

857
00:33:10,345 --> 00:33:11,447
(Servo emulating buzzer)

858
00:33:11,447 --> 00:33:12,555
- Friends to the end, Ilya.

859
00:33:12,555 --> 00:33:14,090
Your steed beside my own.

860
00:33:14,090 --> 00:33:15,886
- Now let us make a pledge.

861
00:33:15,886 --> 00:33:17,836
We shall be as brothers, the three of us.

862
00:33:17,836 --> 00:33:19,434
The younger brother shall heed the elder,

863
00:33:19,434 --> 00:33:21,140
and together we shall venture forth.

864
00:33:21,140 --> 00:33:23,501
- Together, in good and in bad, we three.

865
00:33:23,501 --> 00:33:25,196
- All for one and one for all.

866
00:33:25,196 --> 00:33:26,474
This must be our way.

867
00:33:26,474 --> 00:33:30,109
Our country we shall defend
with our lives if we must.

868
00:33:30,109 --> 00:33:32,026
- Bravo, Ilya Morometz!

869
00:33:32,026 --> 00:33:34,485
- [Crowd] Bravo, Ilya Morometz!

870
00:33:34,485 --> 00:33:37,022
- Put on the armor of a noble, Ilya.

871
00:33:37,022 --> 00:33:38,445
You have earned it.

872
00:33:38,445 --> 00:33:40,306
I thank you, prince.

873
00:33:40,306 --> 00:33:41,699
- Bad tidings, o prince.

874
00:33:41,699 --> 00:33:44,646
Kalin's envoys have
arrived at the city gates.

875
00:33:44,646 --> 00:33:47,221
- [Crow] We got a great big envoy.

876
00:33:47,221 --> 00:33:49,971
- [Servo] Pavarotti tour is in town.

877
00:33:49,971 --> 00:33:51,605
(triumphant music, cheering)

878
00:33:51,605 --> 00:33:54,000
- [Mike] Close the buffet.

879
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,662
- [Servo] Wah-wah-wah.

880
00:33:55,662 --> 00:33:58,174
- [Mike] He's gonna blow!

881
00:33:58,174 --> 00:34:00,365
- Greet them with bread and salt.

882
00:34:00,365 --> 00:34:02,751
Those swine who laid waste our land!

883
00:34:02,751 --> 00:34:04,267
I would rather greet them with arms,

884
00:34:04,267 --> 00:34:06,017
than with bread and salt, sire.

885
00:34:06,017 --> 00:34:08,149
- Those are very cold words, Ilya.

886
00:34:08,149 --> 00:34:10,616
Would you teach me how to rule?

887
00:34:10,616 --> 00:34:12,568
First, we shall hear this envoy.

888
00:34:12,568 --> 00:34:14,688
Then we shall decide what course to take.

889
00:34:14,688 --> 00:34:15,612
- [Mike] All right.

890
00:34:15,612 --> 00:34:17,848
If that's how you wanna do it.

891
00:34:17,848 --> 00:34:19,871
(evocative music)

892
00:34:19,871 --> 00:34:23,207
- [Servo] Sounds like
the stripper's on next.

893
00:34:23,207 --> 00:34:25,770
- [Crow] Somebody get me a
bucket, I'm gonna fro up.

894
00:34:25,770 --> 00:34:28,681
- I come as an envoy from
the mighty Chief Kalin.

895
00:34:28,681 --> 00:34:32,202
It is his will that you shall
pay him taxes and tributes.

896
00:34:32,202 --> 00:34:34,795
For 12 years you must
pay these tributes to us,

897
00:34:34,795 --> 00:34:38,345
else we will invade your
land and empty your coffers.

898
00:34:38,345 --> 00:34:40,087
- [Mike] Damn liberals.

899
00:34:40,087 --> 00:34:42,144
- [Prince] Eat and drink your fill.

900
00:34:42,144 --> 00:34:43,758
We shall pay what you ask.

901
00:34:43,758 --> 00:34:44,591
We shall do it--

902
00:34:44,591 --> 00:34:45,908
- [Servo] Here's your appetizer, sir.

903
00:34:45,908 --> 00:34:47,501
(crashing)

904
00:34:47,501 --> 00:34:51,023
- Kalin's envoy are not to be
bribed with bread and salt.

905
00:34:51,023 --> 00:34:53,599
- To send such a dolt as
an envoy is an insult.

906
00:34:53,599 --> 00:34:55,951
- Does he not look like
a great fat ox to you?

907
00:34:55,951 --> 00:34:58,370
- Who dares speaks thus to Kalin's envoy?

908
00:34:58,370 --> 00:35:00,791
I would strike him down
as soon as look at him.

909
00:35:00,791 --> 00:35:02,647
Guard your tongue or I'll cut it off.

910
00:35:02,647 --> 00:35:04,680
- You come here with words of war.

911
00:35:04,680 --> 00:35:06,260
Therefore, we answer in kind.

912
00:35:06,260 --> 00:35:07,605
And we are prepared.

913
00:35:07,605 --> 00:35:09,477
- Resistance is useless.

914
00:35:09,477 --> 00:35:11,627
I will make you bow to our mighty

915
00:35:11,627 --> 00:35:12,551
chief Kalin.
- [Ilya] The words

916
00:35:12,551 --> 00:35:14,968
of your boasting shall die in your throat,

917
00:35:14,968 --> 00:35:16,171
envoy of Kalin.

918
00:35:16,171 --> 00:35:17,747
- I've heard enough!

919
00:35:17,747 --> 00:35:20,009
Your head should be the first I chop off!

920
00:35:20,009 --> 00:35:21,666
(swooshing, clang, crashing)

921
00:35:21,666 --> 00:35:24,216
- [Mike] Oh, it's a
Matt Groening gargoyle.

922
00:35:24,216 --> 00:35:26,299
- By your own sword, dog,

923
00:35:29,297 --> 00:35:30,130
you shall die!

924
00:35:30,130 --> 00:35:30,963
(swooshing)

925
00:35:30,963 --> 00:35:31,796
Kalin!

926
00:35:31,796 --> 00:35:32,906
- [Crow] Oh, right in the love handle!

927
00:35:32,906 --> 00:35:35,101
- [Servo] Jake and Fatman is
different than I remember.

928
00:35:35,101 --> 00:35:37,027
- [Mike] Jake and the Fatman.

929
00:35:37,027 --> 00:35:39,372
(women screaming)

930
00:35:39,372 --> 00:35:40,517
- [Servo] Woo.

931
00:35:40,517 --> 00:35:43,214
- [Mike] Uh, anyone know
why we're retreating?

932
00:35:43,214 --> 00:35:44,722
- Run, cursed dogs!

933
00:35:44,722 --> 00:35:46,456
Run back to your master, Kalin!

934
00:35:46,456 --> 00:35:47,836
- [Crow] Yeah, babies!

935
00:35:47,836 --> 00:35:50,535
- The same fate awaits anyone he sends us!

936
00:35:50,535 --> 00:35:52,131
Tell him we will fight!

937
00:35:52,131 --> 00:35:54,334
We will pay no tribute!

938
00:35:54,334 --> 00:35:55,548
(crowd cheering)

939
00:35:55,548 --> 00:35:57,435
- [Servo] Our buffets are safe again.

940
00:35:57,435 --> 00:35:58,268
Woo, woo!

941
00:36:01,546 --> 00:36:04,100
- Come wash your hands, o noble soldier.

942
00:36:04,100 --> 00:36:05,077
- [Crow] They're filthy.

943
00:36:05,077 --> 00:36:06,436
- He is indeed a mighty warrior.

944
00:36:06,436 --> 00:36:07,741
As mighty as Durbar.

945
00:36:07,741 --> 00:36:09,418
- And as courageous as Alexei is.

946
00:36:09,418 --> 00:36:11,306
- His strength exceeds that of Invincor.

947
00:36:11,306 --> 00:36:12,747
- For your gallantry,

948
00:36:12,747 --> 00:36:14,443
I will forge for you a coat of armor

949
00:36:14,443 --> 00:36:16,532
finer than the prince's own coat of gold.

950
00:36:16,532 --> 00:36:17,639
- [Mike] Yeah, sure you will.

951
00:36:17,639 --> 00:36:18,531
- Take this lance.

952
00:36:18,531 --> 00:36:19,971
It was forged for a mighty warrior.

953
00:36:19,971 --> 00:36:21,236
- [Crow] He never claimed it.

954
00:36:21,236 --> 00:36:22,798
- I thank you all, good people.

955
00:36:22,798 --> 00:36:23,631
- [Mike] I'm outta here.

956
00:36:23,631 --> 00:36:27,081
- I shall try to be worthy of your trust.

957
00:36:27,081 --> 00:36:27,914
- [Servo] The royal pants!

958
00:36:27,914 --> 00:36:29,928
- Make way for the prince!

959
00:36:29,928 --> 00:36:32,030
- [Crow] Fabulous, the prince!

960
00:36:32,030 --> 00:36:34,089
(triumphant music)

961
00:36:34,089 --> 00:36:38,256
- [Mike] Woo, it's warmer than
I thought it was out here.

962
00:36:39,440 --> 00:36:41,424
- For your service to our people.

963
00:36:41,424 --> 00:36:42,795
- [Servo] It's dry clean only.

964
00:36:42,795 --> 00:36:44,409
- All hail Ilya Morometz.

965
00:36:44,409 --> 00:36:46,195
(crowd cheering)

966
00:36:46,195 --> 00:36:47,785
(all three grunting)

967
00:36:47,785 --> 00:36:50,692
- [Servo] We need lighter heroes.

968
00:36:50,692 --> 00:36:53,271
- [Crow] Oh, once again, I'm not invited.

969
00:36:53,271 --> 00:36:55,108
Finland is so cliquey.

970
00:36:55,108 --> 00:36:56,588
- I must act quickly.

971
00:36:56,588 --> 00:36:58,479
I must get rid of this new hero.

972
00:36:58,479 --> 00:37:00,795
Or else, I will have to answer for myself,

973
00:37:00,795 --> 00:37:03,450
to Kalin and his terrible
band of cutthroats.

974
00:37:03,450 --> 00:37:05,050
- [Servo] Thanks for the aside.

975
00:37:05,050 --> 00:37:08,050
(MST3K theme music)

976
00:37:11,595 --> 00:37:13,205
- And here is your share.

977
00:37:13,205 --> 00:37:14,113
All of this.

978
00:37:14,113 --> 00:37:16,099
All the gold for you, here.

979
00:37:16,099 --> 00:37:17,229
(maniacal laughter)

980
00:37:17,229 --> 00:37:18,509
And now for my share.

981
00:37:18,509 --> 00:37:19,902
- [Servo] Microsoft stock. (chuckling)

982
00:37:19,902 --> 00:37:21,515
- I will take what is left,

983
00:37:21,515 --> 00:37:22,846
the captive maid

984
00:37:22,846 --> 00:37:25,302
who stands there waiting anxiously for me.

985
00:37:25,302 --> 00:37:26,495
(maniacal laughter)

986
00:37:26,495 --> 00:37:27,495
- [Soldier 1] Let me have her

987
00:37:27,495 --> 00:37:29,034
and you can have all my silver!

988
00:37:29,034 --> 00:37:31,248
- [Soldier 2] You can have all my gold.

989
00:37:31,248 --> 00:37:32,264
- Not so fast!

990
00:37:32,264 --> 00:37:33,232
- [Servo] Ooh.

991
00:37:33,232 --> 00:37:35,711
- You shall not have her, nor you.

992
00:37:35,711 --> 00:37:39,256
I will take the captive
maid to Chief Kalin.

993
00:37:39,256 --> 00:37:40,089
- [Servo] Yo.

994
00:37:40,089 --> 00:37:42,244
- He is sure to give me half a kingdom

995
00:37:42,244 --> 00:37:43,747
for this prize beauty.

996
00:37:43,747 --> 00:37:45,801
- [Servo] Exit, stage left.

997
00:37:45,801 --> 00:37:47,670
- It will never be,
you plundering thieves!

998
00:37:47,670 --> 00:37:48,655
- [Crow] Gypsies and tramps!

999
00:37:48,655 --> 00:37:50,700
- [Ilya] She will be set free!

1000
00:37:50,700 --> 00:37:52,781
To go home to her parents.

1001
00:37:52,781 --> 00:37:54,389
- [Mike] Uh, I'm tryin' to sleep.

1002
00:37:54,389 --> 00:37:55,662
- Fear not, little one.

1003
00:37:55,662 --> 00:37:57,193
They shall harm you no longer.

1004
00:37:57,193 --> 00:37:58,573
I shall release you.

1005
00:37:58,573 --> 00:38:00,393
Nothing on this earth.

1006
00:38:00,393 --> 00:38:01,803
- [Servo] Just let me say goodbye to Glok.

1007
00:38:01,803 --> 00:38:05,970
- Not even a Tougar would
keep you from me ever again.

1008
00:38:09,153 --> 00:38:10,219
- The prince!

1009
00:38:10,219 --> 00:38:11,659
- [Crow] Look busy!

1010
00:38:11,659 --> 00:38:13,612
- I see you are quarreling again,

1011
00:38:13,612 --> 00:38:15,086
my rich and worthy nobles.

1012
00:38:15,086 --> 00:38:16,299
- [Mike] So just give me the remote.

1013
00:38:16,299 --> 00:38:17,506
- If I give you free reign,

1014
00:38:17,506 --> 00:38:20,062
you will tear our country
apart with your fighting.

1015
00:38:20,062 --> 00:38:21,312
Matthew Vardoa.

1016
00:38:22,442 --> 00:38:24,651
- [Crow] (sobbing) You're
gonna hit me, aren't you?

1017
00:38:24,651 --> 00:38:25,598
- I have work for you.

1018
00:38:25,598 --> 00:38:28,977
You must prepare a caravan
of furs and copper.

1019
00:38:28,977 --> 00:38:29,841
- [Mike] I'm dead.

1020
00:38:29,841 --> 00:38:31,351
- And voyage out to sea.

1021
00:38:31,351 --> 00:38:32,184
- Sure.

1022
00:38:32,184 --> 00:38:34,845
I wasn't doin' anything
for the next 10 years.

1023
00:38:34,845 --> 00:38:36,556
(birds chirping)

1024
00:38:36,556 --> 00:38:37,502
- [Servo] Song of the South!

1025
00:38:37,502 --> 00:38:41,669
(woman singing in foreign language)

1026
00:38:43,237 --> 00:38:44,743
- [Crow] Woo, Free bird!

1027
00:38:44,743 --> 00:38:45,576
Come back!

1028
00:38:46,819 --> 00:38:47,652
Woo!

1029
00:38:51,563 --> 00:38:55,646
(woman singing, Servo mimicking)

1030
00:38:57,248 --> 00:39:01,651
- [Crow] (chuckling) Ah, dinner.

1031
00:39:01,651 --> 00:39:04,407
- [Servo] Johnny Mercer
lyrics really make this song.

1032
00:39:04,407 --> 00:39:07,903
- [Mike] She did all the same
stuff at her last concert.

1033
00:39:07,903 --> 00:39:11,327
- [Crow] Okay, we all drop on three.

1034
00:39:11,327 --> 00:39:14,565
(birds chirping)

1035
00:39:14,565 --> 00:39:15,979
It's a living!

1036
00:39:15,979 --> 00:39:18,345
- [Mike] Hey, I've got a baby to deliver.

1037
00:39:18,345 --> 00:39:22,512
- [Servo] I'd rather be
roadkill than listen to this.

1038
00:39:24,409 --> 00:39:26,242
How 'bout a tip, lady?

1039
00:39:27,776 --> 00:39:30,341
- [Mike] Well, I gotta
go spread the plague.

1040
00:39:30,341 --> 00:39:31,174
Bye.

1041
00:39:34,682 --> 00:39:37,607
- [Servo] Ah, the magic of
Heidi, ladies and gentlemen!

1042
00:39:37,607 --> 00:39:39,604
(woman singing in foreign language)

1043
00:39:39,604 --> 00:39:43,354
- [Crow] This song
contains satonic messages!

1044
00:39:44,522 --> 00:39:46,066
- [Servo] Hey, Redd Foxx!

1045
00:39:46,066 --> 00:39:47,877
(all three chuckling)

1046
00:39:47,877 --> 00:39:48,710
- [Crow] Ha! Bunny Rich!

1047
00:39:48,710 --> 00:39:52,710
(Mike groaning, Crow chuckling)

1048
00:39:53,939 --> 00:39:56,224
- Still spinning and
weaving, Delia, my love?

1049
00:39:56,224 --> 00:39:57,588
- [Mike] What's with the oven mitts?

1050
00:39:57,588 --> 00:40:00,110
- It has been lonely here without you.

1051
00:40:00,110 --> 00:40:03,452
- I too have spent many years
of loneliness, my dear wife.

1052
00:40:03,452 --> 00:40:05,346
But that is all behind me now.

1053
00:40:05,346 --> 00:40:06,871
I am lonely no more.

1054
00:40:06,871 --> 00:40:07,704
- [Servo] I got a cat.

1055
00:40:07,704 --> 00:40:08,537
- In our marriage,
(romantic music)

1056
00:40:08,537 --> 00:40:10,831
I have found true
happiness, dearest Delia.

1057
00:40:10,831 --> 00:40:12,513
A priceless gift.

1058
00:40:12,513 --> 00:40:15,187
- [Mike] Now, where the hell's my dinner?

1059
00:40:15,187 --> 00:40:17,010
- But what is this?

1060
00:40:17,010 --> 00:40:18,529
- [Servo] How much did this cost?

1061
00:40:18,529 --> 00:40:19,612
- This cloth.

1062
00:40:20,728 --> 00:40:22,242
It's woven of gold, it glitters.

1063
00:40:22,242 --> 00:40:24,124
- It is not a cloth.

1064
00:40:24,124 --> 00:40:26,001
It is a magic tablecloth.

1065
00:40:26,001 --> 00:40:26,908
- [Crow] Uh-huh?

1066
00:40:26,908 --> 00:40:28,378
- It is beautiful, indeed.

1067
00:40:28,378 --> 00:40:29,655
For whom did you make it?

1068
00:40:29,655 --> 00:40:30,615
- [Servo] Deb's wedding shower.

1069
00:40:30,615 --> 00:40:33,617
- For the one whom I love the best.

1070
00:40:33,617 --> 00:40:35,067
- [Crow] The milkman?

1071
00:40:35,067 --> 00:40:38,107
- Now you must rest from your
labors, my busy little wife.

1072
00:40:38,107 --> 00:40:39,212
- [Servo] And dost the nasty do.

1073
00:40:39,212 --> 00:40:40,712
All these wonders.

1074
00:40:41,590 --> 00:40:45,731
The earth offers it
all for us to glory in.

1075
00:40:45,731 --> 00:40:49,814
- [Mike] A beautiful sunset
in Branson, Missouri.

1076
00:40:52,040 --> 00:40:54,636
(Crow mumbling)

1077
00:40:54,636 --> 00:40:56,120
- [Servo] Hey, it's the Nina, the Pinta,

1078
00:40:56,120 --> 00:41:00,287
and Mongol-Santamaria. (chuckling)

1079
00:41:01,604 --> 00:41:04,043
- [Crow] (wolf-whistling) You can almost

1080
00:41:04,043 --> 00:41:05,460
see her hairline.
- [Ilya] Weep not,

1081
00:41:05,460 --> 00:41:07,922
my sweet one, weep not.

1082
00:41:07,922 --> 00:41:10,063
We do not part for long.

1083
00:41:10,063 --> 00:41:10,896
- [Mike] I know.

1084
00:41:10,896 --> 00:41:12,020
That's what I'm grieving about.

1085
00:41:12,020 --> 00:41:14,553
- I shall drive Kalin
and his wicked Tougars

1086
00:41:14,553 --> 00:41:17,742
from the gates of our
city once and for all.

1087
00:41:17,742 --> 00:41:20,888
And rid our land of those
traitors who have betraywed.

1088
00:41:20,888 --> 00:41:22,245
- [Servo] Okay, see ya after work.

1089
00:41:22,245 --> 00:41:24,232
- In this most bitter hour of our parting,

1090
00:41:24,232 --> 00:41:26,528
tell me, dearest one.

1091
00:41:26,528 --> 00:41:28,201
- [Crow] Can I have the checkbook?

1092
00:41:28,201 --> 00:41:30,244
- Tell me truly of your greatest wish.

1093
00:41:30,244 --> 00:41:31,941
- [Servo] Pudding, lots of pudding.

1094
00:41:31,941 --> 00:41:34,285
- Bear me a son, Delia.

1095
00:41:34,285 --> 00:41:35,932
A brave son.

1096
00:41:35,932 --> 00:41:38,302
To grow up strong and be a great warrior.

1097
00:41:38,302 --> 00:41:40,651
- [Crow] Merlin Olsen is no action hero.

1098
00:41:40,651 --> 00:41:42,533
- The falcons in the sky.

1099
00:41:42,533 --> 00:41:45,479
They were witness to
our love, little Delia.

1100
00:41:45,479 --> 00:41:47,536
- [All Three] Euwwww.

1101
00:41:47,536 --> 00:41:51,797
- If you should bear a son,
call him Little Falcon.

1102
00:41:51,797 --> 00:41:52,834
- [Servo] How 'bout Rick?

1103
00:41:52,834 --> 00:41:54,593
- And whenever I see a falcon.

1104
00:41:54,593 --> 00:41:56,156
- [Crow] Um, something.

1105
00:41:56,156 --> 00:41:57,984
- I shall think of my son.

1106
00:41:57,984 --> 00:41:59,529
- It is my greatest wish

1107
00:41:59,529 --> 00:42:02,711
to give you the son
you desire, my beloved.

1108
00:42:02,711 --> 00:42:04,212
- If you bear a son.

1109
00:42:04,212 --> 00:42:06,199
- [Crow] I want to know who the father is.

1110
00:42:06,199 --> 00:42:07,527
- Give him this ring.

1111
00:42:07,527 --> 00:42:09,027
It was given to me

1112
00:42:11,037 --> 00:42:12,504
by our prince.

1113
00:42:12,504 --> 00:42:15,758
- [Mike] Oh, he's gonna give
her his letter jacket, too.

1114
00:42:15,758 --> 00:42:16,768
- [Crow] That's enough now.

1115
00:42:16,768 --> 00:42:19,268
We're being too demonstrative.

1116
00:42:20,399 --> 00:42:23,155
- [Servo] ♫ And now, to Eden ♫

1117
00:42:23,155 --> 00:42:24,869
- [Voiceover] Once again,

1118
00:42:24,869 --> 00:42:27,817
Delia was to be separated from her love.

1119
00:42:27,817 --> 00:42:29,627
- [Mike] She came over last
night and we just talked.

1120
00:42:29,627 --> 00:42:32,522
- [Voiceover] Ilya, fearing
another attack by the Tougars,

1121
00:42:32,522 --> 00:42:35,087
insisted that his wife
accompany the prince's caravan

1122
00:42:35,087 --> 00:42:38,286
of furs and cover.
(Delia singing)

1123
00:42:38,286 --> 00:42:40,690
- [Mike] The Gene Simmons boat.

1124
00:42:40,690 --> 00:42:42,687
- [Voiceover] Delia
would be safe from harm.

1125
00:42:42,687 --> 00:42:45,021
- [Crow] Her singing would
keep everyone at bay.

1126
00:42:45,021 --> 00:42:48,288
(Delia singing in foreign language)

1127
00:42:48,288 --> 00:42:50,475
- [Servo] Nice autoharp.

1128
00:42:50,475 --> 00:42:53,808
Hey, lady, you're puttin' the mast down.

1129
00:42:57,056 --> 00:42:59,691
- [Mike] Wanna grab an
oar, Nana Mouskouri?

1130
00:42:59,691 --> 00:43:03,858
(Delia singing in foreign language)

1131
00:43:07,179 --> 00:43:09,073
(soldiers yelling)

1132
00:43:09,073 --> 00:43:09,906
- [Servo] Humph.

1133
00:43:09,906 --> 00:43:10,800
Boy, he can whip up a horde

1134
00:43:10,800 --> 00:43:13,443
faster than you can say Jack Robinson.

1135
00:43:13,443 --> 00:43:15,482
- [Mike] No, the other way!

1136
00:43:15,482 --> 00:43:16,315
Aagh.

1137
00:43:17,805 --> 00:43:20,888
(all three mumbling)

1138
00:43:23,248 --> 00:43:24,732
(soldiers yelling)

1139
00:43:24,732 --> 00:43:26,053
- [Man] The Tougars are coming!

1140
00:43:26,053 --> 00:43:27,205
- [Servo] The British are coming?

1141
00:43:27,205 --> 00:43:28,312
- No, save me!

1142
00:43:28,312 --> 00:43:29,145
They're coming!

1143
00:43:29,145 --> 00:43:29,978
- [Man] Turn the boat!

1144
00:43:29,978 --> 00:43:32,015
- [Servo] The Navy SEALs are here.

1145
00:43:32,015 --> 00:43:35,848
(soldiers clamoring, yelling)

1146
00:43:38,059 --> 00:43:41,809
- [Crow] Hi, I'm Julie,
your cruise director.

1147
00:43:42,862 --> 00:43:43,838
(soldier exclaiming)

1148
00:43:43,838 --> 00:43:45,577
- [Servo] Hey, you nicked me!

1149
00:43:45,577 --> 00:43:46,785
(Delia exclaiming)

1150
00:43:46,785 --> 00:43:48,759
- [Mike] Come to Uncle Mongol.

1151
00:43:48,759 --> 00:43:49,992
(Servo chuckling)

1152
00:43:49,992 --> 00:43:51,029
- By the gods, here she is again.

1153
00:43:51,029 --> 00:43:52,717
That pretty one for Kalin, ah.

1154
00:43:52,717 --> 00:43:55,948
(all three mumbling)

1155
00:43:55,948 --> 00:43:59,540
(triumphant music, cheering)

1156
00:43:59,540 --> 00:44:02,656
- [Servo] The Magnificent Torklesons!

1157
00:44:02,656 --> 00:44:05,793
- [Mike] Greetings from Rosemary Clooney.

1158
00:44:05,793 --> 00:44:06,904
- [Servo] ♫ Here comes a king

1159
00:44:06,904 --> 00:44:09,175
♫ Here comes a big number one

1160
00:44:09,175 --> 00:44:10,659
♫ Dum-dum-dum-dum ♫

1161
00:44:10,659 --> 00:44:13,885
- [Crow] Ritreck Simulated Film Snow.

1162
00:44:13,885 --> 00:44:15,401
Ask for it by name.
(Servo chuckling)

1163
00:44:15,401 --> 00:44:17,770
- [Servo] ♫ Doo-doo-doo-do-too-loo ♫

1164
00:44:17,770 --> 00:44:19,999
♫ We're cold, we're freezing ♫

1165
00:44:19,999 --> 00:44:21,947
- [Crow And Servo] ♫ We're freezing ♫

1166
00:44:21,947 --> 00:44:24,864
(peasants singing)

1167
00:44:26,355 --> 00:44:29,355
(MST3K theme music)

1168
00:44:32,975 --> 00:44:35,655
♫ Applesauce, balderdash and baloney

1169
00:44:35,655 --> 00:44:38,002
♫ Flim-flam, foodle-diddle, fodge

1170
00:44:38,002 --> 00:44:40,470
♫ Hogwash, hooey and horse feathers

1171
00:44:40,470 --> 00:44:43,077
♫ Pif-pall, pish-posh,
poppycock, pete-and-pete

1172
00:44:43,077 --> 00:44:45,821
♫ Ya, sure, you betcha

1173
00:44:45,821 --> 00:44:49,329
♫ Lutefisk, Lutheran, blatterin' bumpkin

1174
00:44:49,329 --> 00:44:52,183
♫ Flibbertigibbet, ooh-wee, Dwight Yoakam

1175
00:44:52,183 --> 00:44:54,929
♫ Oh, wang-doodle, wing-bag-weep

1176
00:44:54,929 --> 00:44:59,797
♫ Nickety-nack now ♫

1177
00:44:59,797 --> 00:45:01,797
- You guys are so weird.

1178
00:45:04,238 --> 00:45:05,321
- But...

1179
00:45:05,321 --> 00:45:07,433
But I'm a bunny.

1180
00:45:07,433 --> 00:45:09,344
Hop, hop. Hop.

1181
00:45:09,344 --> 00:45:10,512
- [Servo] Oh, give it up.

1182
00:45:10,512 --> 00:45:12,717
- [Crow] Hey, I'm moving, movie sign!

1183
00:45:12,717 --> 00:45:14,355
- [Servo] That's the most
humiliating thing I've ever done.

1184
00:45:14,355 --> 00:45:17,855
(metal clanging, buzzing)

1185
00:45:21,167 --> 00:45:23,334
(beeping)

1186
00:45:26,577 --> 00:45:27,899
- [Mike] Hop, hop, hop.

1187
00:45:27,899 --> 00:45:28,965
Dig on the this thing.

1188
00:45:28,965 --> 00:45:29,955
Hop, hop, hop.

1189
00:45:29,955 --> 00:45:31,455
- Matthew Bredova.

1190
00:45:32,539 --> 00:45:33,943
- [Servo] You're not
wearing that, are you?

1191
00:45:33,943 --> 00:45:35,239
- What is wrong?

1192
00:45:35,239 --> 00:45:37,507
- [Servo] I'm cold and
I'm wet and I wanna go in.

1193
00:45:37,507 --> 00:45:39,531
- Punish me not, o prince.

1194
00:45:39,531 --> 00:45:41,629
Please let me speak first.

1195
00:45:41,629 --> 00:45:43,865
- [Crow] Okay, now punish me.

1196
00:45:43,865 --> 00:45:45,773
- [Prince] Speak, then!

1197
00:45:45,773 --> 00:45:47,521
- We were attacked.

1198
00:45:47,521 --> 00:45:48,354
- [Mike] Woo-hoo!

1199
00:45:48,354 --> 00:45:49,858
- By a band of Tougars.

1200
00:45:49,858 --> 00:45:50,972
- [Crow And Mike] Wee-hee!

1201
00:45:50,972 --> 00:45:52,587
- [Mike] Ooh-hoo.

1202
00:45:52,587 --> 00:45:54,555
- They took everything.

1203
00:45:54,555 --> 00:45:55,388
I escaped.

1204
00:45:56,381 --> 00:45:58,334
After spending months in bondage.

1205
00:45:58,334 --> 00:46:01,010
- [Crow] That was the good part.

1206
00:46:01,010 --> 00:46:04,161
- [Servo] And the Snow Days
Festival was going so well.

1207
00:46:04,161 --> 00:46:05,828
- Ilya Morometz, ah?

1208
00:46:07,241 --> 00:46:08,077
- [Mike] That's Italian.

1209
00:46:08,077 --> 00:46:09,411
- Why was he not there to help?

1210
00:46:09,411 --> 00:46:11,310
- Did I not tell you, radiant prince?

1211
00:46:11,310 --> 00:46:12,513
- He is a fool.

1212
00:46:12,513 --> 00:46:15,176
He is not the sort of
man to be trusted, sire.

1213
00:46:15,176 --> 00:46:18,364
He should have been there to help Matthew.

1214
00:46:18,364 --> 00:46:20,607
- For this, I will banish
him from the court.

1215
00:46:20,607 --> 00:46:22,101
For three full years.

1216
00:46:22,101 --> 00:46:24,710
- [Crow] Throw down your hot dogs.

1217
00:46:24,710 --> 00:46:28,403
- If you banish Ilya,
you exile our strength.

1218
00:46:28,403 --> 00:46:29,420
- Fond as I am of Ilya.

1219
00:46:29,420 --> 00:46:30,299
- [Servo] I hate him.

1220
00:46:30,299 --> 00:46:31,491
- This must be done.

1221
00:46:31,491 --> 00:46:34,217
He goes to the dungeon
to pay for his deed.

1222
00:46:34,217 --> 00:46:37,899
- [Mike] Executive
producer, Steven Bochco.

1223
00:46:37,899 --> 00:46:39,977
- [Ilya] Greetings to you, good soldiers.

1224
00:46:39,977 --> 00:46:40,830
- [Mike] Hi.

1225
00:46:40,830 --> 00:46:42,651
- [Ilya] I see you serve our city well.

1226
00:46:42,651 --> 00:46:45,236
- There is little joy in our
service today I fear, Ilya.

1227
00:46:45,236 --> 00:46:46,561
- [Servo] I gotta work.

1228
00:46:46,561 --> 00:46:48,319
- Blame us not, Ilya.

1229
00:46:48,319 --> 00:46:50,411
The prince has given orders.

1230
00:46:50,411 --> 00:46:51,613
You're not to enter.

1231
00:46:51,613 --> 00:46:53,356
- You jest, do you not?

1232
00:46:53,356 --> 00:46:55,594
I have ridden here in great haste

1233
00:46:55,594 --> 00:46:58,555
to help rid the palace of its traitors!

1234
00:46:58,555 --> 00:47:00,569
- Do not let him in the palace!

1235
00:47:00,569 --> 00:47:01,939
- [Mike] Not with his shoes on!

1236
00:47:01,939 --> 00:47:03,155
- The prince's orders.

1237
00:47:03,155 --> 00:47:04,353
- This is your work,

1238
00:47:04,353 --> 00:47:06,178
o captor of the wind demon,

1239
00:47:06,178 --> 00:47:08,619
so brave and fearless in battle, huh?

1240
00:47:08,619 --> 00:47:13,600
Delia has told me the true
story, traitorous villain!

1241
00:47:13,600 --> 00:47:14,767
- [Servo] D'oh!

1242
00:47:14,767 --> 00:47:16,387
- Ilya, you're not wanted here anymore.

1243
00:47:16,387 --> 00:47:17,901
You have been banished.

1244
00:47:17,901 --> 00:47:21,011
- So, you all conspire
against me, do you, my nobles?

1245
00:47:21,011 --> 00:47:22,188
- [Crow] Let me just,

1246
00:47:22,188 --> 00:47:23,353
hold on.
- [Ilya] You will soon see

1247
00:47:23,353 --> 00:47:24,723
how I deal with conspirators.

1248
00:47:24,723 --> 00:47:26,161
- [Mike] Dig this.

1249
00:47:26,161 --> 00:47:27,586
(swooshing, crashing)

1250
00:47:27,586 --> 00:47:28,586
- [Servo] He does gutter work!

1251
00:47:28,586 --> 00:47:29,754
- [First Noble] I think
he should be hanged

1252
00:47:29,754 --> 00:47:30,587
soon as possible.

1253
00:47:30,587 --> 00:47:32,426
- [Second Noble] I think he
should be drawn and quartered.

1254
00:47:32,426 --> 00:47:35,159
- [Third Noble] Let the prince
decide what to do with him!

1255
00:47:35,159 --> 00:47:37,254
- If the prince wants no more of me,

1256
00:47:37,254 --> 00:47:39,822
then I want no more of his gifts,

1257
00:47:39,822 --> 00:47:41,834
you may tell him.
(Crow wolf-whistling)

1258
00:47:41,834 --> 00:47:42,667
- [Servo] Hmm.

1259
00:47:42,667 --> 00:47:44,783
- As I drag this coat in the
snow by its dangling sleeves.

1260
00:47:44,783 --> 00:47:45,707
- [Mike] It gets filthy.

1261
00:47:45,707 --> 00:47:47,332
- So I shall drag those traitors

1262
00:47:47,332 --> 00:47:49,634
who have plotted against me!

1263
00:47:49,634 --> 00:47:51,695
- [Crow] Here, and no starch!

1264
00:47:51,695 --> 00:47:54,552
- You nobles are ready
enough to join in at peace.

1265
00:47:54,552 --> 00:47:56,573
What about the Tougars, huh?

1266
00:47:56,573 --> 00:47:59,033
Who among you is ready
to stand up and fight

1267
00:47:59,033 --> 00:48:00,364
when the Tougars come?

1268
00:48:00,364 --> 00:48:01,931
- They are brave men, they are,

1269
00:48:01,931 --> 00:48:03,642
when the Tougars are far away.

1270
00:48:03,642 --> 00:48:05,896
- I will drive every
traitor from the palace.

1271
00:48:05,896 --> 00:48:07,450
I swear it!

1272
00:48:07,450 --> 00:48:09,391
- You act too hastily, brother warrior.

1273
00:48:09,391 --> 00:48:10,337
- [Servo] Hmm?

1274
00:48:10,337 --> 00:48:12,271
- The prince is quick of temper,
but he cools quickly too.

1275
00:48:12,271 --> 00:48:13,259
He has sent me to fetch you.

1276
00:48:13,259 --> 00:48:14,368
Come to the palace with me.

1277
00:48:14,368 --> 00:48:16,807
- My honor is at stake!

1278
00:48:16,807 --> 00:48:17,640
I'll not rest

1279
00:48:17,640 --> 00:48:19,175
til I've exposed these scoundrels!

1280
00:48:19,175 --> 00:48:20,279
(soldiers cheering)

1281
00:48:20,279 --> 00:48:22,237
- [Crow] He's consulting
with Black Oak Arkansas.

1282
00:48:22,237 --> 00:48:26,404
- Have you forgotten the
pledge we took, Ilya Morometz?

1283
00:48:27,566 --> 00:48:29,983
The younger brother shall heed the elder?

1284
00:48:29,983 --> 00:48:31,216
That was our pledge, Ilya.

1285
00:48:31,216 --> 00:48:34,791
- Our prince is wise and
knows whom to send here.

1286
00:48:34,791 --> 00:48:36,812
No one could persuade me
to go but you, Durbar.

1287
00:48:36,812 --> 00:48:38,324
- [Servo] Dove Bar?
(Mike chuckling)

1288
00:48:38,324 --> 00:48:40,504
- Come, let us go to the palace now.

1289
00:48:40,504 --> 00:48:42,653
- [Servo] Mmm. (smacking lips)

1290
00:48:42,653 --> 00:48:44,108
- [Mike] Anyway, on Melrose Place.

1291
00:48:44,108 --> 00:48:44,974
Oh, no more.

1292
00:48:44,974 --> 00:48:48,697
- Why did you draw your bow
in anger beneath my window?

1293
00:48:48,697 --> 00:48:50,561
- To avenge the wrong you did

1294
00:48:50,561 --> 00:48:52,612
in accusing me unjustly, sire.

1295
00:48:52,612 --> 00:48:54,174
- The arrow did not leave his bow.

1296
00:48:54,174 --> 00:48:56,359
- He has evil thoughts of you, o prince.

1297
00:48:56,359 --> 00:48:57,722
I saw him trample your coat

1298
00:48:57,722 --> 00:48:59,294
on the ground thusly

1299
00:48:59,294 --> 00:49:01,414
and threaten to do the same to you, sire.

1300
00:49:01,414 --> 00:49:02,870
- Yes, I heard him threaten to that--

1301
00:49:02,870 --> 00:49:04,099
- Yes, he did it, it's right!

1302
00:49:04,099 --> 00:49:05,501
- [Servo] You're outta order!

1303
00:49:05,501 --> 00:49:07,472
The whole damn castle's outta order!

1304
00:49:07,472 --> 00:49:11,245
- But I did not threaten you, my prince.

1305
00:49:11,245 --> 00:49:12,973
- [Man 1] He is not to be trusted, sire.

1306
00:49:12,973 --> 00:49:15,347
- He will stir the entire
court into mutiny, sire!

1307
00:49:15,347 --> 00:49:17,886
- [Crow] There's a little
matter of an unauthorized fax!

1308
00:49:17,886 --> 00:49:19,325
(crowd jeering in distance)

1309
00:49:19,325 --> 00:49:20,158
- Listen.

1310
00:49:20,158 --> 00:49:22,242
Already, they are rebellious.

1311
00:49:22,242 --> 00:49:23,438
- It is not in the streets

1312
00:49:23,438 --> 00:49:25,601
that treachery is planned, o my prince.

1313
00:49:25,601 --> 00:49:26,864
- [Mike] It's at a Chili's.

1314
00:49:26,864 --> 00:49:29,986
- It is right here in the
palace that it is hidden.

1315
00:49:29,986 --> 00:49:32,211
- Your words are empty, Ilya.

1316
00:49:32,211 --> 00:49:33,729
They are untrue.

1317
00:49:33,729 --> 00:49:35,559
- What shall we do with this traitor.

1318
00:49:35,559 --> 00:49:37,878
- Away with him to the dungeons.

1319
00:49:37,878 --> 00:49:39,192
Feed him bread and water.

1320
00:49:39,192 --> 00:49:40,588
- [Crow] Uh, then a salad.

1321
00:49:40,588 --> 00:49:41,421
Then an appetizer.

1322
00:49:41,421 --> 00:49:44,775
- In this way he will
learn humility and wisdom.

1323
00:49:44,775 --> 00:49:45,608
- Prince Vanda,

1324
00:49:45,608 --> 00:49:47,936
I thank you for inviting
me to feast with you.

1325
00:49:47,936 --> 00:49:51,725
And you too, Durbar, for
persuading me to come.

1326
00:49:51,725 --> 00:49:52,789
- I always believed you

1327
00:49:52,789 --> 00:49:54,103
to be on the side of justice, my prince.

1328
00:49:54,103 --> 00:49:55,184
Let Ilya go free.

1329
00:49:55,184 --> 00:49:57,218
- He boasted that he
would rule our country.

1330
00:49:57,218 --> 00:49:59,135
- The deed is done now.

1331
00:50:00,326 --> 00:50:01,818
Lead him away.

1332
00:50:01,818 --> 00:50:04,143
(men clamoring, Servo mumbling)

1333
00:50:04,143 --> 00:50:05,797
- [Man 2] Take him to the dungeon!

1334
00:50:05,797 --> 00:50:06,911
- [Mike] You know, it would be easy

1335
00:50:06,911 --> 00:50:08,429
to grab the wrong whiskery fat guy.

1336
00:50:08,429 --> 00:50:09,728
(Crow chuckling)

1337
00:50:09,728 --> 00:50:10,561
- If I so willed,

1338
00:50:10,561 --> 00:50:12,433
I could have crumbled
your palace into bits,

1339
00:50:12,433 --> 00:50:16,302
but I had no wish to
spoil its decorations.

1340
00:50:16,302 --> 00:50:19,818
The hour will come, Prince Vanda,

1341
00:50:19,818 --> 00:50:21,772
when you will bow to me.

1342
00:50:21,772 --> 00:50:24,008
- [Crow] I can be such a bitch.

1343
00:50:24,008 --> 00:50:24,841
- Now.

1344
00:50:25,744 --> 00:50:28,661
Lead me away, lackeys and schemers.

1345
00:50:29,611 --> 00:50:32,286
I am weary of this talk.
(dramatic music)

1346
00:50:32,286 --> 00:50:36,453
- [Servo] ♫ Everybody's talkin' at me

1347
00:50:38,561 --> 00:50:39,476
Doo-doo-do-do-doo ♫

1348
00:50:39,476 --> 00:50:40,798
- It is not Ilya Morometz
you have wronged,

1349
00:50:40,798 --> 00:50:41,895
but the country herself.

1350
00:50:41,895 --> 00:50:43,635
You have taken the sword from her hand.

1351
00:50:43,635 --> 00:50:45,152
- He speaks the truth!

1352
00:50:45,152 --> 00:50:47,045
We swear never to set foot in the palace.

1353
00:50:47,045 --> 00:50:48,372
- [Servo] Don't we?

1354
00:50:48,372 --> 00:50:50,656
- You have banished us as well.

1355
00:50:50,656 --> 00:50:53,347
- [Crow] Finland's annual
emotional outburst.

1356
00:50:53,347 --> 00:50:56,426
- [Servo] Uh, all for one and one for all?

1357
00:50:56,426 --> 00:50:57,343
Hmm, hello.

1358
00:50:58,187 --> 00:51:01,020
- [Mike] I'll be in my ready room.

1359
00:51:02,084 --> 00:51:03,875
(foreboding music)

1360
00:51:03,875 --> 00:51:06,161
- [Crow] Oh, I hate this thing.

1361
00:51:06,161 --> 00:51:07,730
It does not make me feel pretty.

1362
00:51:07,730 --> 00:51:09,700
- What you have done is
most unwise, my dear.

1363
00:51:09,700 --> 00:51:10,816
Let him go free.

1364
00:51:10,816 --> 00:51:12,744
Send him away to a village.

1365
00:51:12,744 --> 00:51:15,161
He has performed many services for

1366
00:51:15,161 --> 00:51:17,266
our country, dear.
- [Servo] My perky wife.

1367
00:51:17,266 --> 00:51:19,154
- Feed him well, mind you.

1368
00:51:19,154 --> 00:51:21,042
- [Mike] Spread some papers.

1369
00:51:21,042 --> 00:51:22,310
Give 'im a chew toy.

1370
00:51:22,310 --> 00:51:23,575
- He will repent.

1371
00:51:23,575 --> 00:51:24,638
- That country bumpkin

1372
00:51:24,638 --> 00:51:26,476
thinks himself higher than the prince.

1373
00:51:26,476 --> 00:51:27,613
He's much too proud.

1374
00:51:27,613 --> 00:51:28,958
He will never repent.

1375
00:51:28,958 --> 00:51:30,863
- Feed him well, I tell you.

1376
00:51:30,863 --> 00:51:32,913
Feed him well, I command it!

1377
00:51:32,913 --> 00:51:34,852
- [Servo] So they fed him ice
(dramatic music)

1378
00:51:34,852 --> 00:51:36,276
and water.

1379
00:51:36,276 --> 00:51:37,696
- [Crow] Oh, the ice seems safe.

1380
00:51:37,696 --> 00:51:40,279
Let's drive our pickup onto it.

1381
00:51:41,895 --> 00:51:46,062
- [Mike] Yes, Finland is a
four-season vacation paradise.

1382
00:51:47,736 --> 00:51:48,783
- [Servo] I always get put

1383
00:51:48,783 --> 00:51:50,428
right next to the ice machine. (chuckling)

1384
00:51:50,428 --> 00:51:51,810
- [Mike] July in Minnesota.

1385
00:51:51,810 --> 00:51:54,378
(all chuckling)

1386
00:51:54,378 --> 00:51:55,500
- [Crow] Okay, we get it.

1387
00:51:55,500 --> 00:51:57,750
The cycle of friggin' life.

1388
00:51:58,962 --> 00:52:01,962
- [Crow] I think it's a film on sex.

1389
00:52:02,999 --> 00:52:04,965
- Feed him well, he tells me.

1390
00:52:04,965 --> 00:52:07,220
- [Mike] This legend could've
used some punching up.

1391
00:52:07,220 --> 00:52:11,387
- [Servo] The Legend of
Boggy Creek had more depth.

1392
00:52:13,079 --> 00:52:15,720
- That I have not done, nor will I.

1393
00:52:15,720 --> 00:52:17,622
- [Mike] Just empty the chamber pot.

1394
00:52:17,622 --> 00:52:19,668
- He must've died of hunger.

1395
00:52:19,668 --> 00:52:21,668
Seven moons have passed.

1396
00:52:22,629 --> 00:52:24,804
I must send the signal to Sartac.

1397
00:52:24,804 --> 00:52:26,622
Now, swift river, you must help.

1398
00:52:26,622 --> 00:52:28,095
Carry my message to the Tougars

1399
00:52:28,095 --> 00:52:29,727
who wait this promised signal

1400
00:52:29,727 --> 00:52:32,477
which will be the sign to attack.

1401
00:52:34,120 --> 00:52:36,322
- [Servo] I love you, fish.
(splashing)

1402
00:52:36,322 --> 00:52:37,429
- Hey!

1403
00:52:37,429 --> 00:52:40,405
What are you doing up there, eh?

1404
00:52:40,405 --> 00:52:42,130
- Uh, oh, heaven help me.

1405
00:52:42,130 --> 00:52:43,445
There was someone down there.

1406
00:52:43,445 --> 00:52:44,834
- [Crow] Oh, oh, I'm Robin Wiliams.

1407
00:52:44,834 --> 00:52:46,271
Oh, oh, ho!

1408
00:52:46,271 --> 00:52:49,447
- [Mike] Oh, I could go my
whole life without seein' that.

1409
00:52:49,447 --> 00:52:52,101
(whimsical music)

1410
00:52:52,101 --> 00:52:56,134
- [Servo] ♫ And they call
him the streak (whistles) ♫

1411
00:52:56,134 --> 00:52:58,551
- [Crow] I smell fresh pants!

1412
00:52:59,580 --> 00:53:02,317
- [Servo] I'll make myself a
soup out of these trousers.

1413
00:53:02,317 --> 00:53:04,150
- Ah, this is strange.

1414
00:53:05,381 --> 00:53:07,093
I set a trap for a fox,

1415
00:53:07,093 --> 00:53:10,192
I catch a pair of breeches instead.

1416
00:53:10,192 --> 00:53:11,736
- [Mike] Now I am folding them.

1417
00:53:11,736 --> 00:53:13,479
And now I am holding this up.

1418
00:53:13,479 --> 00:53:15,189
- This key looks familiar.

1419
00:53:15,189 --> 00:53:17,022
I have seen it before.

1420
00:53:18,515 --> 00:53:20,774
- [Servo] Bending over now.

1421
00:53:20,774 --> 00:53:23,357
- Ah, this looks like trickery.

1422
00:53:24,565 --> 00:53:26,849
The devil is a sly one.

1423
00:53:26,849 --> 00:53:28,331
But I can play tricks, too.
(Mike chuckling)

1424
00:53:28,331 --> 00:53:31,009
- [Mike] Hey, you don't
need to convince us.

1425
00:53:31,009 --> 00:53:33,184
- [Crow] Wacky prop comic, Lutefisk Top!

1426
00:53:33,184 --> 00:53:34,558
- Whereever you like.

1427
00:53:34,558 --> 00:53:35,576
- [Servo] Whoa.

1428
00:53:35,576 --> 00:53:37,116
- Where the tide takes you.

1429
00:53:37,116 --> 00:53:38,690
Beyond the seven seas!

1430
00:53:38,690 --> 00:53:39,860
- [Servo] Yeah, this scene

1431
00:53:39,860 --> 00:53:43,581
sure brings the film into sharp focus.

1432
00:53:43,581 --> 00:53:45,998
- Joyous news, o exalted one.

1433
00:53:46,900 --> 00:53:48,315
- [Mike] I'm a bird, go away.

1434
00:53:48,315 --> 00:53:50,110
- These patching merchants
have told me of the prince.

1435
00:53:50,110 --> 00:53:51,207
- [Servo] Got my headphones on!

1436
00:53:51,207 --> 00:53:53,494
- He has thrown Morometz into a prison,

1437
00:53:53,494 --> 00:53:56,311
but all the nobles are deserting for home,

1438
00:53:56,311 --> 00:53:58,863
and refusing to fight. (chuckling)

1439
00:53:58,863 --> 00:54:01,153
(Crow, Mike and Servo mimicking laughter)

1440
00:54:01,153 --> 00:54:02,869
- You bring good news.

1441
00:54:02,869 --> 00:54:06,078
I'll destroy the infidel
who dares defy me.

1442
00:54:06,078 --> 00:54:07,649
- [Crow] It's Boris Badenov!

1443
00:54:07,649 --> 00:54:09,810
- Saddle the horses!

1444
00:54:09,810 --> 00:54:10,815
(triumphant music)

1445
00:54:10,815 --> 00:54:12,375
- [Mike] It's Siegfried and Roy.

1446
00:54:12,375 --> 00:54:16,959
- [Servo] Get that horse
outta my living room.

1447
00:54:16,959 --> 00:54:19,190
- The signal, we have just found it,

1448
00:54:19,190 --> 00:54:20,225
in the river,

1449
00:54:20,225 --> 00:54:21,912
he kept his word, that sly one.

1450
00:54:21,912 --> 00:54:23,893
This was the signal we arranged.

1451
00:54:23,893 --> 00:54:26,109
Once again, Kalin, I served you well.

1452
00:54:26,109 --> 00:54:27,249
- Let me see what you have.

1453
00:54:27,249 --> 00:54:28,749
- [Mike] Drop 'em.

1454
00:54:29,758 --> 00:54:31,147
(suctioning sound)

1455
00:54:31,147 --> 00:54:32,725
- He sent a pants-o-gram.

1456
00:54:32,725 --> 00:54:34,395
- [Crow] I ordered heather!

1457
00:54:34,395 --> 00:54:36,258
- By Beelzebub!

1458
00:54:36,258 --> 00:54:37,841
A pair of breeches!

1459
00:54:38,821 --> 00:54:41,207
- [Crow] These pants have
stirred something deep inside me.

1460
00:54:41,207 --> 00:54:43,315
- What does it signify to you?

1461
00:54:43,315 --> 00:54:47,171
- [Mike] It signifies
the man had a large can.

1462
00:54:47,171 --> 00:54:48,369
(Servo chuckling)

1463
00:54:48,369 --> 00:54:50,309
- They are ready to surrender to Kalin.

1464
00:54:50,309 --> 00:54:51,549
- [Servo] Ha.

1465
00:54:51,549 --> 00:54:54,288
Blossom was really funny last night.

1466
00:54:54,288 --> 00:54:55,598
- These breeches are a symbol

1467
00:54:55,598 --> 00:54:57,752
of the unconquerable might of Kalin.

1468
00:54:57,752 --> 00:54:59,213
- [Crow] And we'll take them in!

1469
00:54:59,213 --> 00:55:01,613
- Each ready to herald

1470
00:55:01,613 --> 00:55:03,969
the power and the glory that is Kalin.

1471
00:55:03,969 --> 00:55:07,615
- [Mike] I don't know what
I'm talkin' about here.

1472
00:55:07,615 --> 00:55:08,669
- Two roads here.

1473
00:55:08,669 --> 00:55:11,602
And both of them will
lead Kalin to victory.

1474
00:55:11,602 --> 00:55:14,685
- Yes, victory shall be ours finally.

1475
00:55:15,584 --> 00:55:19,305
- [Servo] Ah, the golden
age of makin' stuff up.

1476
00:55:19,305 --> 00:55:21,928
- The attack must be timed
according to the stars.

1477
00:55:21,928 --> 00:55:22,761
- You are correct.

1478
00:55:22,761 --> 00:55:23,909
- [Crow] Sir!

1479
00:55:23,909 --> 00:55:25,394
- It is not yet time to attack

1480
00:55:25,394 --> 00:55:27,688
until the gods of battle tell us.

1481
00:55:27,688 --> 00:55:29,606
We will bide our time.

1482
00:55:29,606 --> 00:55:31,282
- [Servo] We will wear our pants.

1483
00:55:31,282 --> 00:55:33,292
- Unsaddle all the horses.

1484
00:55:33,292 --> 00:55:34,459
- [Mike] Okay!

1485
00:55:35,625 --> 00:55:38,498
- [Voiceover] And while Kalin
waited for a favorable sign,

1486
00:55:38,498 --> 00:55:41,748
Ilya Morometz rotted in a dark dungeon,

1487
00:55:42,596 --> 00:55:45,207
unaware that his wife had borne the son

1488
00:55:45,207 --> 00:55:47,124
he so fervently wanted.

1489
00:55:48,257 --> 00:55:49,090
- [Servo] Oh.

1490
00:55:49,090 --> 00:55:51,415
- [Voiceover] And so
the months slipped by.

1491
00:55:51,415 --> 00:55:52,595
- [Servo] Like a pair of pants.

1492
00:55:52,595 --> 00:55:54,698
- You are still only a baby,

1493
00:55:54,698 --> 00:55:56,726
and already stronger than an oak.

1494
00:55:56,726 --> 00:55:57,922
- [Crow] And dumber than a hammer.

1495
00:55:57,922 --> 00:56:00,066
- Well, my son, grow tall and strong.

1496
00:56:00,066 --> 00:56:01,579
And be like your father.

1497
00:56:01,579 --> 00:56:03,569
- [Mike] I'm tryin'. (grunting)

1498
00:56:03,569 --> 00:56:04,402
Eh.

1499
00:56:04,402 --> 00:56:05,472
- Courage like his.

1500
00:56:05,472 --> 00:56:07,168
- [Servo] But I wanna watch Power Rangers.

1501
00:56:07,168 --> 00:56:08,001
- And strength, as well.

1502
00:56:08,001 --> 00:56:09,590
- [Mike] Can I get some
breakfast, or what?

1503
00:56:09,590 --> 00:56:11,170
- Little Falcon, my son.

1504
00:56:11,170 --> 00:56:14,146
This is your present from him.

1505
00:56:14,146 --> 00:56:17,563
- [Crow] Is my face as weird as it feels?

1506
00:56:18,419 --> 00:56:20,752
- [Servo] Burgers are ready!

1507
00:56:25,929 --> 00:56:27,179
- [Servo] Well?

1508
00:56:28,199 --> 00:56:31,234
- [Mike] Kiss your Aunt Bernice.

1509
00:56:31,234 --> 00:56:34,117
- Run along and play, little one.

1510
00:56:34,117 --> 00:56:34,950
- [Servo] Thanks.

1511
00:56:34,950 --> 00:56:35,833
What's the draw strength on this thing?

1512
00:56:35,833 --> 00:56:37,916
Could I take down an elk?

1513
00:56:38,886 --> 00:56:40,309
- Why do you not love me?

1514
00:56:40,309 --> 00:56:41,380
- [Mike] You look like RuPaul.

1515
00:56:41,380 --> 00:56:43,499
- Why do you run away?

1516
00:56:43,499 --> 00:56:45,228
How many times must I tell you?

1517
00:56:45,228 --> 00:56:46,926
I wish to keep you for my own.

1518
00:56:46,926 --> 00:56:48,595
- Never, I despise you!

1519
00:56:48,595 --> 00:56:50,958
- [Crow] He has an outie
in the middle of his head.

1520
00:56:50,958 --> 00:56:52,095
- [Servo] Who loves ya, baby?

1521
00:56:52,095 --> 00:56:53,431
- You shall never touch me, Kalin,

1522
00:56:53,431 --> 00:56:55,011
I swear it on my life!

1523
00:56:55,011 --> 00:56:57,454
What manner of man are you to force me?

1524
00:56:57,454 --> 00:56:59,140
- [Kalin] Kings grovel at my feet.

1525
00:56:59,140 --> 00:57:00,546
And so will you, my dear.

1526
00:57:00,546 --> 00:57:04,156
- I would sooner you throw me
into a cage of wild animals!

1527
00:57:04,156 --> 00:57:05,341
- [Mike] Hmm, done and done.

1528
00:57:05,341 --> 00:57:07,015
- You will never have me.

1529
00:57:07,015 --> 00:57:08,108
(Kalin laughing maniacally)

1530
00:57:08,108 --> 00:57:09,024
- [Crow] I do need a father, Mom.

1531
00:57:09,024 --> 00:57:10,845
(Delia exclaiming, thud)

1532
00:57:10,845 --> 00:57:11,850
- I will kill you!

1533
00:57:11,850 --> 00:57:13,639
- [Servo] For God and country, uh-oh.

1534
00:57:13,639 --> 00:57:15,666
- Ah, the little wolf cub.

1535
00:57:15,666 --> 00:57:19,417
He fights, huh? (laughing)

1536
00:57:19,417 --> 00:57:21,187
- [Mike] I got it handled, Mom.

1537
00:57:21,187 --> 00:57:24,854
(Delia exclaiming, sobbing)

1538
00:57:26,188 --> 00:57:27,021
- [Servo] What?

1539
00:57:27,021 --> 00:57:27,854
I'm a Mongol!

1540
00:57:27,854 --> 00:57:30,362
- I shall teach you how to fight.

1541
00:57:30,362 --> 00:57:31,218
And your enemy shall be the cursed prince.

1542
00:57:31,218 --> 00:57:32,187
- [Crow] Sound all right?

1543
00:57:32,187 --> 00:57:34,937
(dramatic music)

1544
00:57:35,959 --> 00:57:38,406
- [Servo] Uncle BO, can
I shoot you in the back?

1545
00:57:38,406 --> 00:57:41,606
(arrow wooshing, landing)

1546
00:57:41,606 --> 00:57:42,607
- [Crow] Ow!

1547
00:57:42,607 --> 00:57:44,119
- [Mike] Frampton comes alive.

1548
00:57:44,119 --> 00:57:45,043
(arrow swooshing, landing)

1549
00:57:45,043 --> 00:57:45,876
- [Servo] Ow!

1550
00:57:45,876 --> 00:57:46,709
Jeez.

1551
00:57:46,709 --> 00:57:47,542
- [Crow] I've never hit a damn thing.

1552
00:57:47,542 --> 00:57:48,567
It's astounding!

1553
00:57:48,567 --> 00:57:50,367
- You are still a boy, Little Falcon,

1554
00:57:50,367 --> 00:57:52,808
and already you have the
strength of a warrior.

1555
00:57:52,808 --> 00:57:55,406
You shall challenge our
champion to a jousting bout.

1556
00:57:55,406 --> 00:57:57,797
- [Mike] We'll put in on pay-per-view.

1557
00:57:57,797 --> 00:58:01,224
- [Kilan] Show us, Little
Falcon, whom I call my son,

1558
00:58:01,224 --> 00:58:03,567
how skillfully you wield a lance.

1559
00:58:03,567 --> 00:58:04,400
- [Crow] Michael Keaton!

1560
00:58:04,400 --> 00:58:06,684
- [Kilan] I know I shall be proud of you.

1561
00:58:06,684 --> 00:58:08,372
(triumphant music)

1562
00:58:08,372 --> 00:58:12,230
- [Servo] The Tower of
Gourds horn section!

1563
00:58:12,230 --> 00:58:14,813
- [Mike] Whatta I do with this?

1564
00:58:16,589 --> 00:58:19,236
(crowd cheering, opponent laughing)

1565
00:58:19,236 --> 00:58:21,883
- [Crow] Ha, hat's funny!

1566
00:58:21,883 --> 00:58:22,920
Where's he goin'?

1567
00:58:22,920 --> 00:58:23,753
Jerry!

1568
00:58:28,919 --> 00:58:30,139
That's it?

1569
00:58:30,139 --> 00:58:31,889
I want my money back.

1570
00:58:32,992 --> 00:58:36,031
- [Servo] Shouldn't there be
a dragon around pretty soon?

1571
00:58:36,031 --> 00:58:39,350
(triumphant music)

1572
00:58:39,350 --> 00:58:40,540
(maniacal laughter)

1573
00:58:40,540 --> 00:58:41,386
- [Mike] Whaddaya laugh?

1574
00:58:41,386 --> 00:58:42,219
I don't get it.

1575
00:58:42,219 --> 00:58:43,052
What?

1576
00:58:43,052 --> 00:58:44,429
- To the dungeon with this weakling.

1577
00:58:44,429 --> 00:58:46,144
Let him guard the captives.

1578
00:58:46,144 --> 00:58:48,151
(laughter)

1579
00:58:48,151 --> 00:58:49,880
- [Crow] Sorry, something I ate.

1580
00:58:49,880 --> 00:58:53,390
(horse neighing)

1581
00:58:53,390 --> 00:58:55,156
- [Kalin] Well done, Little Falcon.

1582
00:58:55,156 --> 00:58:58,237
You have earned the cap of
champion to wear as your own.

1583
00:58:58,237 --> 00:59:02,902
- [Servo] Now, Mongolian
stir-fry for everyone!

1584
00:59:02,902 --> 00:59:05,823
- The time has come to take up our arms.

1585
00:59:05,823 --> 00:59:07,156
We move at last.

1586
00:59:08,820 --> 00:59:10,506
(foreboding music)

1587
00:59:10,506 --> 00:59:11,339
- [Crow] Wow.

1588
00:59:11,339 --> 00:59:12,394
Now that is a horde.

1589
00:59:12,394 --> 00:59:14,511
- [Mike] This is a free festival now, man.

1590
00:59:14,511 --> 00:59:18,953
I wish we had the yogurt
franchise for this horde.

1591
00:59:18,953 --> 00:59:20,978
- [Servo] It's kind of Mingus jazzy feel.

1592
00:59:20,978 --> 00:59:24,311
(Servo emulating music)

1593
00:59:26,282 --> 00:59:29,199
- [Mike] Grow, little Mongol horde.

1594
00:59:30,344 --> 00:59:31,737
(crowd cheering)

1595
00:59:31,737 --> 00:59:34,228
- [Servo] A giant pair o'pants back there.

1596
00:59:34,228 --> 00:59:38,145
- [Crow] So, they walked
from China to Finland.

1597
00:59:39,169 --> 00:59:41,072
- [Mike] Are we goin' the right way?

1598
00:59:41,072 --> 00:59:45,251
- [Crow] I'm just following
you, I don't know.

1599
00:59:45,251 --> 00:59:49,557
- [Servo] One guy following
along with a Pooper-Scooper.

1600
00:59:49,557 --> 00:59:51,474
- [Mike] Sounds like a concerto
for tympani and car horn.

1601
00:59:51,474 --> 00:59:53,101
(Servo chuckling)

1602
00:59:53,101 --> 00:59:54,831
- [Crow] I'm goin' to
Helsinki to personally spear

1603
00:59:54,831 --> 00:59:56,526
that stump throwin' son-of-a-bitch.

1604
00:59:56,526 --> 00:59:58,115
- [Servo] Will the
Laurence of Arabia people

1605
00:59:58,115 --> 01:00:00,467
please get to their proper sets?

1606
01:00:00,467 --> 01:00:03,217
(exciting music)

1607
01:00:05,298 --> 01:00:07,780
(Servo humming)

1608
01:00:07,780 --> 01:00:08,761
No, keep it open!

1609
01:00:08,761 --> 01:00:11,024
Oh, great, our plan is ruined.

1610
01:00:11,024 --> 01:00:13,980
- [Soldier 1] Give us 700
carts filled with gold,

1611
01:00:13,980 --> 01:00:18,147
Prince Vanda, or prepare to
surrender yourself as hostage!

1612
01:00:19,196 --> 01:00:20,655
- [Soldier 2] Our might Chief Kalin

1613
01:00:20,655 --> 01:00:23,591
gives you three hours to reply!

1614
01:00:23,591 --> 01:00:27,178
If you refuse, your bones
will bleach in the sun!

1615
01:00:27,178 --> 01:00:28,011
- [Servo] It's a White
Sox pennant, I think.

1616
01:00:28,011 --> 01:00:29,919
- We will take your people captive

1617
01:00:29,919 --> 01:00:32,345
for the pleasure of our chief!

1618
01:00:32,345 --> 01:00:34,514
- [Prince] Give this reply to Kalin.

1619
01:00:34,514 --> 01:00:35,750
(Crow blowing raspberry)

1620
01:00:35,750 --> 01:00:36,813
- [Prince] What you have demanded,

1621
01:00:36,813 --> 01:00:39,497
we will pay you in three days from now.

1622
01:00:39,497 --> 01:00:41,769
- [Mike] We have to call
and clear it with the bank.

1623
01:00:41,769 --> 01:00:43,107
- [Soldier 1] You must bring your tribute

1624
01:00:43,107 --> 01:00:46,058
to Kalin's camp at the river!

1625
01:00:46,058 --> 01:00:47,630
- Well?

1626
01:00:47,630 --> 01:00:50,901
Which of your nobles will
you send to fight them?

1627
01:00:50,901 --> 01:00:52,040
Here they are.

1628
01:00:52,040 --> 01:00:52,873
Choose one.

1629
01:00:52,873 --> 01:00:56,037
(Crow, Mike, and Servo muttering)

1630
01:00:56,037 --> 01:00:57,575
Truly Ilya Morometz,

1631
01:00:57,575 --> 01:01:00,916
when he said there would
be many to feast with you,

1632
01:01:00,916 --> 01:01:04,048
but none to stand up for our land.

1633
01:01:04,048 --> 01:01:05,129
He spoke wisely.

1634
01:01:05,129 --> 01:01:06,827
- [Servo] Any of you
Mongols need another wife?

1635
01:01:06,827 --> 01:01:09,459
- Oh, if only Ilya were with us.

1636
01:01:09,459 --> 01:01:11,347
This Kalin would not keep us in terror.

1637
01:01:11,347 --> 01:01:13,300
- [Crow] A collie is
keeping them in terror.

1638
01:01:13,300 --> 01:01:16,058
- I shall go to him and
ask his forgiveness.

1639
01:01:16,058 --> 01:01:17,991
- Prince, prince!

1640
01:01:17,991 --> 01:01:19,317
He may be dead.

1641
01:01:19,317 --> 01:01:21,287
He has refused food and drink. (mumbles)

1642
01:01:21,287 --> 01:01:22,699
- Why have you kept this from me?

1643
01:01:22,699 --> 01:01:24,454
Open the dungeon!

1644
01:01:24,454 --> 01:01:25,658
You'll pay for this.

1645
01:01:25,658 --> 01:01:26,673
- [Mike] You hold a Finn by the beard,

1646
01:01:26,673 --> 01:01:28,193
it immobilizes him.

1647
01:01:28,193 --> 01:01:29,183
- Wait here, Radiant Prince.

1648
01:01:29,183 --> 01:01:30,481
I must run and fetch the key.

1649
01:01:30,481 --> 01:01:32,624
I do not have it with me.

1650
01:01:32,624 --> 01:01:33,706
- Is this not the key?

1651
01:01:33,706 --> 01:01:36,465
I believe this is the
key to the dungeon, sire.

1652
01:01:36,465 --> 01:01:38,966
- [Servo] We run a damn
confusing kingdom here.

1653
01:01:38,966 --> 01:01:41,966
(MST3K theme music)

1654
01:01:45,971 --> 01:01:47,968
(foreboding music)

1655
01:01:47,968 --> 01:01:49,290
- So, you wily scoundrel.

1656
01:01:49,290 --> 01:01:51,702
You starved him to death, son of misery.

1657
01:01:51,702 --> 01:01:53,297
- [Servo] (snoring)
Hey, I just got to sleep

1658
01:01:53,297 --> 01:01:54,130
after 20 years.

1659
01:01:54,130 --> 01:01:56,986
- [Princess] Look, he is alive, alive!

1660
01:01:56,986 --> 01:01:58,748
- Well, as alive as a Finn gets, anyways.

1661
01:01:58,748 --> 01:02:00,542
- [Prince] He is alive!

1662
01:02:00,542 --> 01:02:01,835
- [Servo] Yeah.

1663
01:02:01,835 --> 01:02:04,616
- I fed him prince, as you commanded.

1664
01:02:04,616 --> 01:02:06,401
- He lies, my prince.

1665
01:02:06,401 --> 01:02:09,486
- He is the traitor who
has plotted against you.

1666
01:02:09,486 --> 01:02:10,712
- [Mike] He's got bedhead.

1667
01:02:10,712 --> 01:02:12,540
- It was this that I came to tell you,

1668
01:02:12,540 --> 01:02:15,352
but I was thrown into
this dark dungeon instead.

1669
01:02:15,352 --> 01:02:17,219
- [Crow] And I wake up
with my beard in my mouth.

1670
01:02:17,219 --> 01:02:18,052
- Not at all.

1671
01:02:18,052 --> 01:02:19,631
He would have died in this dungeon

1672
01:02:19,631 --> 01:02:21,483
without my bread and water.

1673
01:02:21,483 --> 01:02:24,343
- It was my Delia who saved my life.

1674
01:02:24,343 --> 01:02:27,260
Come, I will show you what she did.

1675
01:02:28,898 --> 01:02:31,651
(gentle music)

1676
01:02:31,651 --> 01:02:35,232
- [Servo] ♫ I'll never smile again ♫

1677
01:02:35,232 --> 01:02:36,065
- [Mike] I must warn you,

1678
01:02:36,065 --> 01:02:37,683
I've got a weird scene goin' here.

1679
01:02:37,683 --> 01:02:40,293
- [Princess] A miracle, truly a miracle!

1680
01:02:40,293 --> 01:02:41,689
- [Crow] That's what we need!

1681
01:02:41,689 --> 01:02:44,249
- Forgive me, Ilya, I have wronged you.

1682
01:02:44,249 --> 01:02:46,585
Help us, Ilya, against Kalin.

1683
01:02:46,585 --> 01:02:48,156
- [Ilya] You wish my help, Prince?

1684
01:02:48,156 --> 01:02:49,685
- Ilya, we need you.

1685
01:02:49,685 --> 01:02:51,020
- [Servo] Honey, can I do just one thing?

1686
01:02:51,020 --> 01:02:52,454
- Great danger threatens.

1687
01:02:52,454 --> 01:02:54,606
The Tougars stand at our gates.

1688
01:02:54,606 --> 01:02:55,445
- [Mike] Just two guns?

1689
01:02:55,445 --> 01:02:56,925
- Vast numbers of them.

1690
01:02:56,925 --> 01:02:58,480
- Help us, Ilya.

1691
01:02:58,480 --> 01:02:59,609
- [Crow] Help us.

1692
01:02:59,609 --> 01:03:01,620
- Forget your grievance, Ilya.

1693
01:03:01,620 --> 01:03:02,453
- [Crow] Pete Rose!

1694
01:03:02,453 --> 01:03:04,453
- For the people's sake.

1695
01:03:06,698 --> 01:03:08,617
- [Mike] Well, I thought it over,

1696
01:03:08,617 --> 01:03:09,855
and I will definitely

1697
01:03:09,855 --> 01:03:12,272
not help you, ha-ha-ha-ha-ha!

1698
01:03:14,237 --> 01:03:16,529
- Not for your sake, Prince Vanda,

1699
01:03:16,529 --> 01:03:18,417
nor for the sake of your princess.

1700
01:03:18,417 --> 01:03:22,584
- [Crow] But for the sake of
The New Christy Minstrels.

1701
01:03:23,718 --> 01:03:26,243
- But for the beloved
land which gave me birth,

1702
01:03:26,243 --> 01:03:27,660
and which I love,

1703
01:03:29,822 --> 01:03:31,825
for her will I give my strength.

1704
01:03:31,825 --> 01:03:33,254
- [Servo] For the regular
Joe, tryin' to make a livin'.

1705
01:03:33,254 --> 01:03:34,368
For the farmers!

1706
01:03:34,368 --> 01:03:36,963
- [Prince] For you, Ilya Morometz,

1707
01:03:36,963 --> 01:03:38,091
my golden suit of armor.

1708
01:03:38,091 --> 01:03:38,924
- [Mike] We'll let it out.

1709
01:03:38,924 --> 01:03:41,134
- [Prince] And for that
traitor, the boiling tar.

1710
01:03:41,134 --> 01:03:42,522
- [Crow] With croutons and melted cheese.

1711
01:03:42,522 --> 01:03:44,182
(exclamations of protest)

1712
01:03:44,182 --> 01:03:45,131
- [Mike] You know,

1713
01:03:45,131 --> 01:03:47,643
I'd kinda like to watch the
whole melting tar thing.

1714
01:03:47,643 --> 01:03:48,476
What?

1715
01:03:48,476 --> 01:03:51,231
- Tell me, what do you
think we should do first?

1716
01:03:51,231 --> 01:03:53,617
- There is one thing we must do

1717
01:03:53,617 --> 01:03:55,440
without a moment's delay.

1718
01:03:55,440 --> 01:03:56,461
- [Crow] Let's have lunch.

1719
01:03:56,461 --> 01:03:58,729
- You must summon all of your
fighting men to your side

1720
01:03:58,729 --> 01:04:00,551
to plan the battle at once.

1721
01:04:00,551 --> 01:04:01,661
- [Mike] Do ya love this man?

1722
01:04:01,661 --> 01:04:03,200
I love this man!

1723
01:04:03,200 --> 01:04:04,988
- [Prince] Within three days,

1724
01:04:04,988 --> 01:04:07,139
I will assemble every warrior in the land.

1725
01:04:07,139 --> 01:04:10,137
- [Servo] Just don't get it, do you?

1726
01:04:10,137 --> 01:04:12,927
- [Crow] Well, that didn't work.

1727
01:04:12,927 --> 01:04:14,680
(Servo sniggering)

1728
01:04:14,680 --> 01:04:17,574
- [Servo] I claim this Mongol
for all crows everywhere.

1729
01:04:17,574 --> 01:04:18,446
- [Crow] Crows!

1730
01:04:18,446 --> 01:04:19,746
My brethrens!

1731
01:04:19,746 --> 01:04:21,773
See what a grand and
noble creature they are?

1732
01:04:21,773 --> 01:04:22,606
- [Servo] Uh-huh.

1733
01:04:22,606 --> 01:04:24,375
- [Voiceover] But Kalin's men
were restless for plunder,

1734
01:04:24,375 --> 01:04:26,382
and would not wait.

1735
01:04:26,382 --> 01:04:27,860
And beyond the palace,

1736
01:04:27,860 --> 01:04:29,595
on another plain outside the city,

1737
01:04:29,595 --> 01:04:30,762
they attacked.

1738
01:04:32,438 --> 01:04:33,750
Greatly outnumbered,

1739
01:04:33,750 --> 01:04:36,651
the bold defenders fought back bravely.

1740
01:04:36,651 --> 01:04:37,484
- [Mike] Sort of.

1741
01:04:37,484 --> 01:04:39,918
- [Voiceover] And won the day.

1742
01:04:39,918 --> 01:04:40,751
(stirring music)

1743
01:04:40,751 --> 01:04:41,796
But what of tomorrow?

1744
01:04:41,796 --> 01:04:42,744
- [Servo] Well, I'm gonna sleep in.

1745
01:04:42,744 --> 01:04:44,661
Oh, he means the movie.

1746
01:04:45,643 --> 01:04:46,810
- [Crow] Pyle!

1747
01:04:49,220 --> 01:04:51,647
- [Mike] Please dispose
of your Mongols properly.

1748
01:04:51,647 --> 01:04:54,298
- [Servo] Another Super Fun site is born.

1749
01:04:54,298 --> 01:04:56,366
(horse whinnying)

1750
01:04:56,366 --> 01:04:59,449
- [Crow] Woodstock 2 ends in tragedy.

1751
01:05:00,575 --> 01:05:01,579
- [Mike] The mass effects

1752
01:05:01,579 --> 01:05:03,358
of watching Pauly Shore's last movie.

1753
01:05:03,358 --> 01:05:04,898
- This indeed was a costly battle,

1754
01:05:04,898 --> 01:05:06,584
but we to keep the foe in check.

1755
01:05:06,584 --> 01:05:07,489
- [Servo] Well, I liked it.

1756
01:05:07,489 --> 01:05:09,276
- The prince has wronged us sorely.

1757
01:05:09,276 --> 01:05:10,183
Still we have fought against

1758
01:05:10,183 --> 01:05:11,527
the enemy that threatens him.
- [Servo] Yow-how!

1759
01:05:11,527 --> 01:05:13,856
- And now we must help
him further, Alexei.

1760
01:05:13,856 --> 01:05:16,332
- Not even if the path be
strewn with golden coins.

1761
01:05:16,332 --> 01:05:17,722
I will not fight for him again.

1762
01:05:17,722 --> 01:05:19,008
- We must forget our feelings.

1763
01:05:19,008 --> 01:05:20,831
The prince stands in his greatest danger,

1764
01:05:20,831 --> 01:05:21,935
and he needs us.

1765
01:05:21,935 --> 01:05:24,245
- Would you lead me to the
prince as once you led Ilya?

1766
01:05:24,245 --> 01:05:25,250
For the nobles to jeer at?

1767
01:05:25,250 --> 01:05:28,037
- Do you think I do not
grieve over Ilya as you do,

1768
01:05:28,037 --> 01:05:29,782
grieving over the fate
that has befallen him?

1769
01:05:29,782 --> 01:05:31,194
- [Mike] Shall we dance?

1770
01:05:31,194 --> 01:05:32,882
- Why do you quarrel so?

1771
01:05:32,882 --> 01:05:33,812
- [Servo] Summin' to do.

1772
01:05:33,812 --> 01:05:37,174
- Has the world grown too
narrow for both of you?

1773
01:05:37,174 --> 01:05:39,997
You must hasten to Ilya
Morometz, he is alive.

1774
01:05:39,997 --> 01:05:41,547
I have heard that he lives!

1775
01:05:41,547 --> 01:05:42,380
- [Alexei] He lives?

1776
01:05:42,380 --> 01:05:44,116
- Yes, he is safe and well.

1777
01:05:44,116 --> 01:05:46,286
- [Alexei] This is indeed wondrous.

1778
01:05:46,286 --> 01:05:47,964
- [Crow] Hey!

1779
01:05:47,964 --> 01:05:49,486
(gong clanging)

1780
01:05:49,486 --> 01:05:50,900
(stirring music)

1781
01:05:50,900 --> 01:05:54,891
- [Servo] 'Scuse me,
here, smoke. (coughing)

1782
01:05:54,891 --> 01:05:55,724
Wow.

1783
01:05:58,107 --> 01:06:00,310
- [Crow] Do we all need our own campfires?

1784
01:06:00,310 --> 01:06:05,310
- [Servo] Musta got ahold of
some wet wood, or somethin'.

1785
01:06:05,310 --> 01:06:06,393
Bacon grease.

1786
01:06:09,832 --> 01:06:11,003
- [Mike] Yeah, you got yourself

1787
01:06:11,003 --> 01:06:13,836
quite a view from the patio, Ilya.

1788
01:06:15,482 --> 01:06:19,190
- [Crow] We are gonna get
our butts kicked so bad!

1789
01:06:19,190 --> 01:06:23,079
- [Servo] Well, get used to
Mongolian beef, everybody.

1790
01:06:23,079 --> 01:06:25,938
- [Mike] Uh, is there a
back way outta this place?

1791
01:06:25,938 --> 01:06:29,693
- [Crow] Hey, they took
The Golden Gate Bridge!

1792
01:06:29,693 --> 01:06:32,776
- The three days have already passed.

1793
01:06:34,923 --> 01:06:37,139
Soon, the Tougars will strike again.

1794
01:06:37,139 --> 01:06:38,610
- [Servo] There's a lot more
than two guys out there.

1795
01:06:38,610 --> 01:06:40,715
- And still no sign of our men.

1796
01:06:40,715 --> 01:06:42,492
- I myself shall go to Kalin,

1797
01:06:42,492 --> 01:06:45,435
and persuade him to
grant us three days more.

1798
01:06:45,435 --> 01:06:47,206
- [Mike] Oh, sweetheart, will you?

1799
01:06:47,206 --> 01:06:49,342
- [Prince] Spare neither gold nor silver.

1800
01:06:49,342 --> 01:06:52,825
Fill new sacks to the brim
and load them on gilded carts.

1801
01:06:52,825 --> 01:06:56,632
- Harken to these words from
a simple farmer, my prince.

1802
01:06:56,632 --> 01:07:00,187
We will use torn sacks and
load them on old carts.

1803
01:07:00,187 --> 01:07:01,020
- [Servo] Hmm?

1804
01:07:01,020 --> 01:07:03,853
- We will take but a small
portion of your treasures.

1805
01:07:03,853 --> 01:07:05,922
I have thought out a plan.

1806
01:07:05,922 --> 01:07:08,672
(Servo mumbling)

1807
01:07:10,080 --> 01:07:11,026
- You, ride slowly,

1808
01:07:11,026 --> 01:07:13,562
and drop a jewel on the
ground every 10 paces.

1809
01:07:13,562 --> 01:07:14,958
- [Servo] Ah, drop this old man.

1810
01:07:14,958 --> 01:07:17,386
- And you drop a silver
coin at every hundred paces!

1811
01:07:17,386 --> 01:07:18,691
- [Mike] I'll do it later.

1812
01:07:18,691 --> 01:07:21,027
- And you at every thousand
paces, a golden coin!

1813
01:07:21,027 --> 01:07:22,787
(horse neighing)

1814
01:07:22,787 --> 01:07:23,668
- [Crow] This is great!

1815
01:07:23,668 --> 01:07:25,845
I can't believe how
well my plan is working.

1816
01:07:25,845 --> 01:07:27,365
- I want them.

1817
01:07:27,365 --> 01:07:30,308
I will expect each of you, my warriors,

1818
01:07:30,308 --> 01:07:33,198
to bring home much gold from his palace.

1819
01:07:33,198 --> 01:07:35,344
It shall all be ours.

1820
01:07:35,344 --> 01:07:36,862
- [Mike] I bet you get most of it.

1821
01:07:36,862 --> 01:07:38,362
- All of it, ours.

1822
01:07:41,239 --> 01:07:42,783
(horse whinnying)

1823
01:07:42,783 --> 01:07:44,329
- [Crow] Will you be
more than two hours, sir?

1824
01:07:44,329 --> 01:07:46,333
♫ Dum-dee-dee-de-doom-dee ♫

1825
01:07:46,333 --> 01:07:47,355
- Mighty Chief Kalin!

1826
01:07:47,355 --> 01:07:50,524
Prince Vanda has sent us
here with gifts and bounties

1827
01:07:50,524 --> 01:07:51,521
you have commanded!
- [Mike] Look up there.

1828
01:07:51,521 --> 01:07:53,369
It's the Trix are for kids monument.

1829
01:07:53,369 --> 01:07:55,319
(Kalin laughing)

1830
01:07:55,319 --> 01:07:57,089
- So, the prince has submitted?

1831
01:07:57,089 --> 01:07:59,710
He is wise, your prince.

1832
01:07:59,710 --> 01:08:01,126
- Yes, Kalin.

1833
01:08:01,126 --> 01:08:03,563
Here is all the treasure.

1834
01:08:03,563 --> 01:08:05,699
In the first cart, silver.

1835
01:08:05,699 --> 01:08:07,177
- [Servo] And Nutrageous bars.

1836
01:08:07,177 --> 01:08:09,822
- And this one is filled
with coins of gold.

1837
01:08:09,822 --> 01:08:12,464
And the one beside it
is loaded with jewels.

1838
01:08:12,464 --> 01:08:14,168
- [Crow] And we'll throw the guy in, too.

1839
01:08:14,168 --> 01:08:16,470
- And they're all for you.

1840
01:08:16,470 --> 01:08:17,478
- [Kalin] Unload the carts,

1841
01:08:17,478 --> 01:08:18,864
and fill the gold into my sacks!

1842
01:08:18,864 --> 01:08:20,485
- [Mike] What, you don't like our sacks?

1843
01:08:20,485 --> 01:08:23,485
- [Servo] Uh, paper or plastic, sir?

1844
01:08:26,673 --> 01:08:28,256
Hey, a wheat penny!

1845
01:08:30,579 --> 01:08:31,412
- Aaagh!

1846
01:08:34,168 --> 01:08:35,843
- [Mike] What are they having there?

1847
01:08:35,843 --> 01:08:38,065
A cootie festival?
(Servo chuckling)

1848
01:08:38,065 --> 01:08:40,072
- This is indeed unfortunate.

1849
01:08:40,072 --> 01:08:40,905
You see.

1850
01:08:40,905 --> 01:08:42,522
- [Crow] It's good burlap.

1851
01:08:42,522 --> 01:08:43,355
I don't know what happened.

1852
01:08:43,355 --> 01:08:45,005
- It is quite simple.

1853
01:08:45,005 --> 01:08:47,430
As we prepared to leave the palace walls,

1854
01:08:47,430 --> 01:08:49,123
the prince was in great sorrow,

1855
01:08:49,123 --> 01:08:50,507
as you can understand.

1856
01:08:50,507 --> 01:08:52,809
His riches, he loaded on broken carts,

1857
01:08:52,809 --> 01:08:55,237
and his gold, he poured
into these torn sacks.

1858
01:08:55,237 --> 01:08:58,776
It must all have spilled all the way here.

1859
01:08:58,776 --> 01:09:00,048
- [Servo] You buyin' any o'this?

1860
01:09:00,048 --> 01:09:02,499
- And only these few
pieces of gold are left.

1861
01:09:02,499 --> 01:09:04,287
- [Crow] Well, whaddaya gonna do?

1862
01:09:04,287 --> 01:09:05,120
Humph.

1863
01:09:05,120 --> 01:09:06,715
- Will your men go back for
it or shall I send mine?

1864
01:09:06,715 --> 01:09:08,317
- [Servo] Service is our middle name!

1865
01:09:08,317 --> 01:09:12,075
- I fear if I send mine,
you may not get it all.

1866
01:09:12,075 --> 01:09:15,575
(metal clanging, beeping)

1867
01:09:22,979 --> 01:09:24,438
- [Servo] From downtown!

1868
01:09:24,438 --> 01:09:25,399
Oh, baby!

1869
01:09:25,399 --> 01:09:26,962
- [Crow] You missed some.

1870
01:09:26,962 --> 01:09:29,675
- Hey, something's comin'
in on the hex screen.

1871
01:09:29,675 --> 01:09:32,614
- Hey, it's who-ya-what's-his-face.

1872
01:09:32,614 --> 01:09:34,628
- [Ilya] Yes it is I, Ilya Morometz.

1873
01:09:34,628 --> 01:09:36,606
And behold, I have a new job.

1874
01:09:36,606 --> 01:09:40,153
Here, at the legendary pancake house,

1875
01:09:40,153 --> 01:09:42,403
where I am a waiter, ha-ha!

1876
01:09:43,570 --> 01:09:44,501
Hava cookin'!

1877
01:09:44,501 --> 01:09:47,283
- [Mike] That's great.
(Crow chuckling)

1878
01:09:47,283 --> 01:09:48,116
- [Crow] Yeah.

1879
01:09:48,116 --> 01:09:50,141
- [Ilya] And yet the
day is filled with woe,

1880
01:09:50,141 --> 01:09:51,201
for we are short of staff,

1881
01:09:51,201 --> 01:09:53,082
and my great heart is filled with sadness,

1882
01:09:53,082 --> 01:09:55,582
for I must take Cindy's shift.

1883
01:09:56,524 --> 01:09:58,614
- [Mike] Aw, that's too bad.

1884
01:09:58,614 --> 01:10:02,503
- [Ilya] And yet, little
ones, my heart rejoices.

1885
01:10:02,503 --> 01:10:06,031
For behold, this short
stack of wheat cakes,

1886
01:10:06,031 --> 01:10:06,864
laden with berries,

1887
01:10:06,864 --> 01:10:09,612
and smothered with the
cream which is whipped.

1888
01:10:09,612 --> 01:10:10,898
- [Mike] Mmm.
- [Crow] Yum. (smacks lips)

1889
01:10:10,898 --> 01:10:13,278
- [Ilya] And to accompany,
rashers of bacon,

1890
01:10:13,278 --> 01:10:15,607
and beautiful links of sausage of pork

1891
01:10:15,607 --> 01:10:16,805
for all to rejoice in.
- [Servo] Sausage.

1892
01:10:16,805 --> 01:10:19,107
- [Crow] Or, uh, you could
probably get ham, huh?

1893
01:10:19,107 --> 01:10:19,940
- [Ilya] Ham?

1894
01:10:19,940 --> 01:10:21,861
- Yeah, a little Virginia honey-baked ham?

1895
01:10:21,861 --> 01:10:22,932
Yes!

1896
01:10:22,932 --> 01:10:23,765
- Ooh, yeah.

1897
01:10:23,765 --> 01:10:25,296
- [Ilya] Substitution
is spawn of the devil.

1898
01:10:25,296 --> 01:10:26,264
- [Crow] Well, now, hey!

1899
01:10:26,264 --> 01:10:27,230
Hold on there!

1900
01:10:27,230 --> 01:10:29,242
- [Ilya] Not even a Tougar
shall order off the menu.

1901
01:10:29,242 --> 01:10:30,075
- [Mike] Hey, hey!

1902
01:10:30,075 --> 01:10:30,937
- [Ilya] What?

1903
01:10:30,937 --> 01:10:32,396
- [Mike] Hey, come on.

1904
01:10:32,396 --> 01:10:34,256
You're Ilya Murometz.

1905
01:10:34,256 --> 01:10:35,702
Defender of the realm.

1906
01:10:35,702 --> 01:10:37,698
I mean, accept this challenge.

1907
01:10:37,698 --> 01:10:41,412
Proof to us that you could bring ham!

1908
01:10:41,412 --> 01:10:42,950
- [Crow] Yeah.

1909
01:10:42,950 --> 01:10:43,783
- [Ilya] Yes.

1910
01:10:43,783 --> 01:10:44,616
Yes, yes.

1911
01:10:44,616 --> 01:10:45,449
I will gather my strength,

1912
01:10:45,449 --> 01:10:46,282
and I shall go forth.

1913
01:10:46,282 --> 01:10:47,115
And I shall go to the back.

1914
01:10:47,115 --> 01:10:49,044
And I shall request ham,

1915
01:10:49,044 --> 01:10:51,677
for it is ham that I seek.

1916
01:10:51,677 --> 01:10:53,341
Ham!

1917
01:10:53,341 --> 01:10:54,424
- [Mike] Ham.

1918
01:10:56,454 --> 01:10:57,328
- [Crow] Ham.

1919
01:10:57,328 --> 01:10:58,161
- [Ilya] Ham!

1920
01:10:58,161 --> 01:10:58,994
- [Crow] Good luck!

1921
01:10:58,994 --> 01:10:59,827
- [Mike] Ham, ham.

1922
01:10:59,827 --> 01:11:00,660
Good luck with the ham.

1923
01:11:00,660 --> 01:11:01,595
- [Crow] That stupid
square head. (chuckles)

1924
01:11:01,595 --> 01:11:02,532
- [Mike] Oh, he's not that bad.

1925
01:11:02,532 --> 01:11:03,365
We'll be right back.

1926
01:11:03,365 --> 01:11:04,198
Maybe you're right.

1927
01:11:04,198 --> 01:11:07,198
(MST3K theme music)

1928
01:11:09,650 --> 01:11:10,755
- [Kalin] Well?

1929
01:11:10,755 --> 01:11:13,536
- We search all day for chief
(Crow, Mike, Servo muttering)

1930
01:11:13,536 --> 01:11:14,909
and have found no gold.

1931
01:11:14,909 --> 01:11:16,986
- Put him to his death like a dog!

1932
01:11:16,986 --> 01:11:18,365
- [Servo] What kind of dog, my lord?

1933
01:11:18,365 --> 01:11:20,485
- Do not act in anger, Kalin.

1934
01:11:20,485 --> 01:11:23,801
There is no need to be
hasty about killing me.

1935
01:11:23,801 --> 01:11:26,294
First, you must take the
treasures that are yours.

1936
01:11:26,294 --> 01:11:27,127
- [Soldier] Ugh!

1937
01:11:27,127 --> 01:11:28,256
- [Crow] Hit me!

1938
01:11:28,256 --> 01:11:29,587
(jangling)

1939
01:11:29,587 --> 01:11:31,690
- [Mike] He's got all our spoons.

1940
01:11:31,690 --> 01:11:33,087
(exciting music)

1941
01:11:33,087 --> 01:11:36,754
- [Servo] So, when does
Ilya's plan kick in?

1942
01:11:37,686 --> 01:11:41,019
- [Crow] He's got Dick Butkus intensity.

1943
01:11:42,877 --> 01:11:43,710
- [Servo] Hmm.

1944
01:11:43,710 --> 01:11:44,688
- [Mike] You're mad, aren'tcha?

1945
01:11:44,688 --> 01:11:45,735
You're mad.
(soldier crying out)

1946
01:11:45,735 --> 01:11:46,568
- [Crow] That's telling him, sir.

1947
01:11:46,568 --> 01:11:47,922
Oh, ooh, oof!
(soldier crying out)

1948
01:11:47,922 --> 01:11:49,987
He's worse than Bobby Knight.

1949
01:11:49,987 --> 01:11:51,581
- [Servo] (whispering) No, it's Bob.

1950
01:11:51,581 --> 01:11:54,595
- Whosoever steals from me
will die by my own sword,

1951
01:11:54,595 --> 01:11:56,241
like the dog that he is.

1952
01:11:56,241 --> 01:11:58,045
Come forward, chief warriors!

1953
01:11:58,045 --> 01:11:59,571
- [Mike] He loves that dog thing.

1954
01:11:59,571 --> 01:12:01,552
- Gather every coin and treasure!

1955
01:12:01,552 --> 01:12:03,152
Pile them all at my feet!

1956
01:12:03,152 --> 01:12:05,293
- [Crow] Move it, move it, move it!

1957
01:12:05,293 --> 01:12:09,246
- It is better to give up
the gold than lose our heads.

1958
01:12:09,246 --> 01:12:10,329
(clanging)

1959
01:12:10,329 --> 01:12:11,774
- Empty your pockets, ah.

1960
01:12:11,774 --> 01:12:13,919
The prince shall repay us a thousand fold.

1961
01:12:13,919 --> 01:12:15,153
- Yes, yes.

1962
01:12:15,153 --> 01:12:16,702
Pile all the treasure at my feet.

1963
01:12:16,702 --> 01:12:17,991
Every piece!

1964
01:12:17,991 --> 01:12:18,908
Every coin!

1965
01:12:19,917 --> 01:12:23,917
- [Servo] Oh, that was
gratuitous, Tad, come on.

1966
01:12:25,151 --> 01:12:26,591
Oh, and it goes without saying,

1967
01:12:26,591 --> 01:12:28,924
do it like the dogs you are!

1968
01:12:30,704 --> 01:12:34,454
(Servo emulating soundtrack)

1969
01:12:36,245 --> 01:12:37,078
(maniacal laughter)

1970
01:12:37,078 --> 01:12:39,375
- [Crow] Ah, this is better
than shopping by mail!

1971
01:12:39,375 --> 01:12:42,922
- [Mike] Ilya's plan seems ungainly.

1972
01:12:42,922 --> 01:12:44,198
- [Servo] Ah, yes, Michael Ovitz

1973
01:12:44,198 --> 01:12:46,948
at his monthly managers' meeting.

1974
01:12:50,327 --> 01:12:51,194
- [Crow] Here.

1975
01:12:51,194 --> 01:12:52,424
Hope ya choke on it.

1976
01:12:52,424 --> 01:12:55,250
- [Mike] There goes my
laundry money, you dick weed.

1977
01:12:55,250 --> 01:12:56,083
Fine.

1978
01:12:57,901 --> 01:12:59,406
- [Servo] Thanks to you, it's working.

1979
01:12:59,406 --> 01:13:00,864
The United Way.

1980
01:13:00,864 --> 01:13:02,814
- [Ilya] See Chief Kalin,

1981
01:13:02,814 --> 01:13:05,131
what great riches you have now?

1982
01:13:05,131 --> 01:13:06,795
- But it is not enough.

1983
01:13:06,795 --> 01:13:08,333
- [Crow] I want moose and squirrel.

1984
01:13:08,333 --> 01:13:09,166
- There is one thing to make me content.

1985
01:13:09,166 --> 01:13:11,333
Bring to me Ilya Morometz.

1986
01:13:12,383 --> 01:13:14,341
That is what I'd like.

1987
01:13:14,341 --> 01:13:17,341
Then shall I retreat from your gate.

1988
01:13:19,047 --> 01:13:21,296
- [Ilya] So shall it be, mighty Kalin.

1989
01:13:21,296 --> 01:13:22,665
- [Mike] Yo, baby, you heard him.

1990
01:13:22,665 --> 01:13:23,671
- Return to the palace.

1991
01:13:23,671 --> 01:13:27,645
Go to the dungeon and
seek out Ilya Moromtez,

1992
01:13:27,645 --> 01:13:30,914
and bring him back here
with you to this very place.

1993
01:13:30,914 --> 01:13:31,858
Hurry!

1994
01:13:31,858 --> 01:13:33,056
- [Servo] What is his plan?

1995
01:13:33,056 --> 01:13:34,727
- And tell the prince not to dally.

1996
01:13:34,727 --> 01:13:36,185
There is not a moment to lose.

1997
01:13:36,185 --> 01:13:38,935
Tell him that, do you understand?

1998
01:13:40,482 --> 01:13:41,459
- [Crow] Am I alone here?

1999
01:13:41,459 --> 01:13:42,292
Hello?

2000
01:13:43,951 --> 01:13:44,793
- All mighty chief Kalin.

2001
01:13:44,793 --> 01:13:46,943
We have searched along every road.

2002
01:13:46,943 --> 01:13:48,757
They are not bring Ilya Morometz.

2003
01:13:48,757 --> 01:13:50,512
- [Mike] Oh, and I made
pudding in a skull.

2004
01:13:50,512 --> 01:13:53,262
- You have deceived me, emissary.

2005
01:13:54,626 --> 01:13:55,741
And you shall die.

2006
01:13:55,741 --> 01:13:57,969
- I'm willing to stake my own life on it.

2007
01:13:57,969 --> 01:14:00,318
Ilya Morometz will appear before you.

2008
01:14:00,318 --> 01:14:02,131
- If I had Ilya Morometz before me,

2009
01:14:02,131 --> 01:14:04,648
I would retreat and withdraw my men.

2010
01:14:04,648 --> 01:14:06,628
- Here I stand!

2011
01:14:06,628 --> 01:14:07,531
(crowd gasping)

2012
01:14:07,531 --> 01:14:08,364
- [Servo] He's a disco ball.

2013
01:14:08,364 --> 01:14:09,463
- Ilya Morometz!
(crowd murmuring)

2014
01:14:09,463 --> 01:14:11,142
Now withdraw your men.

2015
01:14:11,142 --> 01:14:14,582
You are band by the promise
you have made to retreat.

2016
01:14:14,582 --> 01:14:16,855
- [Mike] Chad, I have a
big problem with this.

2017
01:14:16,855 --> 01:14:20,150
- You think, perhaps, I am a fool.

2018
01:14:20,150 --> 01:14:22,811
I should chop off your head!

2019
01:14:22,811 --> 01:14:24,638
- [Crow] I had my fingers
crossed all the time.

2020
01:14:24,638 --> 01:14:28,100
- But for the courage you have shown,

2021
01:14:28,100 --> 01:14:30,142
I might pardon you.

2022
01:14:30,142 --> 01:14:32,329
I shall command and you follow.

2023
01:14:32,329 --> 01:14:34,666
My clever emissary.

2024
01:14:34,666 --> 01:14:36,436
You shall be one of us.

2025
01:14:36,436 --> 01:14:40,094
- Never shall I serve a tyrant
or betray my native land!

2026
01:14:40,094 --> 01:14:41,608
We shall fight you to the end,

2027
01:14:41,608 --> 01:14:43,475
until we have regained our freedom.

2028
01:14:43,475 --> 01:14:44,357
- [Servo] No, we won't!

2029
01:14:44,357 --> 01:14:45,753
- Take your men and
retreat at once, tyrant.

2030
01:14:45,753 --> 01:14:49,627
We shall destroy you,
each and every one of you.

2031
01:14:49,627 --> 01:14:51,127
- Agh, tie him up!

2032
01:14:52,111 --> 01:14:54,022
- [Mike] Uh, how's this, uh.

2033
01:14:54,022 --> 01:14:57,256
- I wish him to be burned alive.

2034
01:14:57,256 --> 01:14:58,422
- [Crow] Like a dog, sir?

2035
01:14:58,422 --> 01:14:59,666
- Bring him here to him.

2036
01:14:59,666 --> 01:15:01,893
I shall pull his arm out of its socket!

2037
01:15:01,893 --> 01:15:03,322
Drag him here!

2038
01:15:03,322 --> 01:15:05,178
- With these hands, bloody tyrant,

2039
01:15:05,178 --> 01:15:08,093
I shall crush the breath
from your monstrous body!

2040
01:15:08,093 --> 01:15:08,950
(crashing)

2041
01:15:08,950 --> 01:15:11,725
- [Servo] Houdini lives!

2042
01:15:11,725 --> 01:15:14,073
(whistling)

2043
01:15:14,073 --> 01:15:15,414
- [Crow] Lassie!

2044
01:15:15,414 --> 01:15:19,243
- [Mike] Fooled them into
thinkin' tea was ready.

2045
01:15:19,243 --> 01:15:22,202
- [Servo] Ooh, a real sepia
tone's come over the crowd.

2046
01:15:22,202 --> 01:15:23,283
- After him!

2047
01:15:23,283 --> 01:15:26,159
I want him alive!
(exciting music)

2048
01:15:26,159 --> 01:15:27,073
- Mighty Chief!

2049
01:15:27,073 --> 01:15:28,237
Your allies have fled.

2050
01:15:28,237 --> 01:15:29,791
They refuse to join you and your men

2051
01:15:29,791 --> 01:15:31,269
on the the attack on Prince Vanda.

2052
01:15:31,269 --> 01:15:32,102
- Ah.

2053
01:15:32,102 --> 01:15:33,009
- [Crow] That felt good.

2054
01:15:33,009 --> 01:15:35,709
- You, you must go alone against them.

2055
01:15:35,709 --> 01:15:37,442
And in single combat.

2056
01:15:37,442 --> 01:15:38,767
- [Mike] Ilya's plan is still on.

2057
01:15:38,767 --> 01:15:39,813
Don't give up hope!

2058
01:15:39,813 --> 01:15:40,963
(horse neighing)

2059
01:15:40,963 --> 01:15:43,140
- [Servo] This is
Arthurian in the sense that

2060
01:15:43,140 --> 01:15:45,018
Arthur with Dudley Moore is Arthurian.

2061
01:15:45,018 --> 01:15:46,646
- Ho, ho, ho!

2062
01:15:46,646 --> 01:15:47,985
- [Crow] I mean, hi-diddle-ee-dee!

2063
01:15:47,985 --> 01:15:52,473
- Your strongest man to
meet me in single combat!

2064
01:15:52,473 --> 01:15:54,303
- [Mike] Sunday, Sunday, Sunday!

2065
01:15:54,303 --> 01:15:57,245
- [Servo] Great, my
fruitcake son is calling me.

2066
01:15:57,245 --> 01:16:00,470
- [Ilya] Come, my young
braggart who shouts so loudly.

2067
01:16:00,470 --> 01:16:03,129
I am ready to meet you in single combat.

2068
01:16:03,129 --> 01:16:05,057
- [Falcon] You are too old and feeble.

2069
01:16:05,057 --> 01:16:06,570
You are no match for me!

2070
01:16:06,570 --> 01:16:07,875
Go home, old man.

2071
01:16:07,875 --> 01:16:09,553
- [Crow] Hey, I walk the malls.

2072
01:16:09,553 --> 01:16:12,695
- First kill a falcon, young
man, before you bind him.

2073
01:16:12,695 --> 01:16:14,182
- You are afraid to fight.

2074
01:16:14,182 --> 01:16:16,752
Now I shall show you no mercy, old one!

2075
01:16:16,752 --> 01:16:20,383
(exciting music, swords clanging)

2076
01:16:20,383 --> 01:16:23,584
- [Mike] This movie has the
same plot as A Boy Named Sue.

2077
01:16:23,584 --> 01:16:25,027
- [Crow] Father!

2078
01:16:25,027 --> 01:16:25,936
- [Servo] Yes, son?

2079
01:16:25,936 --> 01:16:27,299
- [Crow] I want to kill you.

2080
01:16:27,299 --> 01:16:28,587
- [Mike] Guys.

2081
01:16:28,587 --> 01:16:29,420
- [Crow] I want--

2082
01:16:29,420 --> 01:16:30,573
- [Mike] Guys.

2083
01:16:30,573 --> 01:16:32,319
- [Servo] This is gonna turn into

2084
01:16:32,319 --> 01:16:34,248
The Guns of Will Sonnett now, isn't it?

2085
01:16:34,248 --> 01:16:37,802
(horse neighing)

2086
01:16:37,802 --> 01:16:41,022
(Crow moaning)

2087
01:16:41,022 --> 01:16:42,579
- Up, you young braggart.

2088
01:16:42,579 --> 01:16:43,412
Up!

2089
01:16:44,601 --> 01:16:46,312
Your strength is great.

2090
01:16:46,312 --> 01:16:49,765
- [Mike] Your odor is powerful, ech.

2091
01:16:49,765 --> 01:16:52,628
- [Servo] I wanna go to art school!

2092
01:16:52,628 --> 01:16:53,670
- [Crow] Nice ring!

2093
01:16:53,670 --> 01:16:55,587
You get that wholesale?

2094
01:16:57,334 --> 01:16:59,028
(grunting)

2095
01:16:59,028 --> 01:17:00,625
- [Mike] Putting this into my plan.

2096
01:17:00,625 --> 01:17:02,860
My plan is very flexible.

2097
01:17:02,860 --> 01:17:04,830
(grunting)

2098
01:17:04,830 --> 01:17:06,984
- Hold, my brave young warrior.

2099
01:17:06,984 --> 01:17:10,316
I had not thought we would ever
meet on the field of battle.

2100
01:17:10,316 --> 01:17:11,481
- Why did you not kill me

2101
01:17:11,481 --> 01:17:12,850
when you could, old man?

2102
01:17:12,850 --> 01:17:14,107
I would've shown you no
mercy were I in your place!

2103
01:17:14,107 --> 01:17:18,178
- Be not so firey, my wild unbroken colt.

2104
01:17:18,178 --> 01:17:19,011
(Servo chuckling)

2105
01:17:19,011 --> 01:17:20,014
Tell me your name, young man.

2106
01:17:20,014 --> 01:17:21,737
And what do they call you?

2107
01:17:21,737 --> 01:17:24,014
Who are your father and mother?

2108
01:17:24,014 --> 01:17:24,847
- I have no mother.

2109
01:17:24,847 --> 01:17:26,748
I have never seen her.

2110
01:17:26,748 --> 01:17:29,168
I am Little Falcon, the son of Kalin.

2111
01:17:29,168 --> 01:17:31,045
- What you say is not true.

2112
01:17:31,045 --> 01:17:32,834
I am your father.

2113
01:17:32,834 --> 01:17:35,003
- [Crow] Oh, great, my dad's Burl Ives.

2114
01:17:35,003 --> 01:17:36,847
- Do you speak the truth, old man?

2115
01:17:36,847 --> 01:17:39,283
- Is this really the truth?

2116
01:17:39,283 --> 01:17:40,912
- Yes, I speak the truth!

2117
01:17:40,912 --> 01:17:43,264
Look no, I will show you.

2118
01:17:43,264 --> 01:17:44,643
- I got a little birthmark
on my left butt cheek.

2119
01:17:44,643 --> 01:17:45,476
- See?

2120
01:17:45,476 --> 01:17:47,261
This is my ring you are wearing.

2121
01:17:47,261 --> 01:17:49,928
- [Mike] You graduated '83, too?

2122
01:17:52,707 --> 01:17:54,669
(serene music)

2123
01:17:54,669 --> 01:17:56,724
- [Servo] Wow, they get the
family channel on the ring.

2124
01:17:56,724 --> 01:18:00,429
- [Mike] It's the little Dutch boy.

2125
01:18:00,429 --> 01:18:04,966
- It is as though in a
vision, I see my mother.

2126
01:18:04,966 --> 01:18:06,245
- [Crow] Mom!

2127
01:18:06,245 --> 01:18:08,041
- Oh, Father.

2128
01:18:08,041 --> 01:18:11,675
Will you ever forgive
me for what I have done?

2129
01:18:11,675 --> 01:18:14,175
- [Servo] Why did you lick me, son?

2130
01:18:14,175 --> 01:18:15,306
(Mike laughing)

2131
01:18:15,306 --> 01:18:16,925
- And now, I wish to
fight with all my power

2132
01:18:16,925 --> 01:18:18,006
for the prince and you.

2133
01:18:18,006 --> 01:18:19,545
- [Mike] Kid's loyalty turns on a dime.

2134
01:18:19,545 --> 01:18:21,299
- No, my son.

2135
01:18:21,299 --> 01:18:22,296
I have plan.

2136
01:18:22,296 --> 01:18:23,134
- [Servo] Oh, no!

2137
01:18:23,134 --> 01:18:25,381
- You must go back and
find your mother, boy.

2138
01:18:25,381 --> 01:18:27,805
You will know her by the
scar on her right cheek

2139
01:18:27,805 --> 01:18:31,637
from the sword of one of Kalin's Tougars.

2140
01:18:31,637 --> 01:18:32,937
(exciting music)

2141
01:18:32,937 --> 01:18:33,830
- [Crow] Kind of a long way, Dad.

2142
01:18:33,830 --> 01:18:35,042
Is there a bus or somethin'?

2143
01:18:35,042 --> 01:18:36,045
- We must pretend to fight.

2144
01:18:36,045 --> 01:18:36,878
They are watching us.

2145
01:18:36,878 --> 01:18:38,919
Strike me, Father, with all your strength!

2146
01:18:38,919 --> 01:18:40,715
- [Servo] Want every penny's worth.

2147
01:18:40,715 --> 01:18:41,622
(thud)

2148
01:18:41,622 --> 01:18:43,542
- [Mike] Jeez, who am I, Gary Crosby?

2149
01:18:43,542 --> 01:18:44,754
- Kill them all!

2150
01:18:44,754 --> 01:18:46,492
Massacre every one of them!

2151
01:18:46,492 --> 01:18:50,024
(Mumbling), spare no one.

2152
01:18:50,024 --> 01:18:53,287
- [Crow] Ilya's plan
moves into phase nine.

2153
01:18:53,287 --> 01:18:55,493
- You will take the left flank, Alexei.

2154
01:18:55,493 --> 01:18:56,523
- [Servo] I like white meat.

2155
01:18:56,523 --> 01:18:59,775
- And Durbar's men will take
follow along the right flank.

2156
01:18:59,775 --> 01:19:02,921
And I will lead my men through
the center of their ranks.

2157
01:19:02,921 --> 01:19:06,624
The prince remains here with
his men to defend the palace.

2158
01:19:06,624 --> 01:19:09,349
- [Mike] Foghat prepares for war.

2159
01:19:09,349 --> 01:19:13,516
(horde exclaiming, bots cheering along)

2160
01:19:15,800 --> 01:19:20,287
- [Servo] We are live from
beautiful Trojan Stadium today!

2161
01:19:20,287 --> 01:19:23,204
(horde exclaiming)

2162
01:19:24,187 --> 01:19:28,354
- [Crow] That is one
Irish-Catholic family! (whistles)

2163
01:19:29,292 --> 01:19:31,244
- [Mike] The cattle
call for Sound of Music.

2164
01:19:31,244 --> 01:19:33,046
- [The Bots] ♫ The hills are alive

2165
01:19:33,046 --> 01:19:35,171
♫ The hills are alive

2166
01:19:35,171 --> 01:19:36,194
♫ With the sound of ♫

2167
01:19:36,194 --> 01:19:37,694
- [Crow] Run away!

2168
01:19:41,263 --> 01:19:45,430
50,000 Maria van Trapps face
off with the Mongol horde!

2169
01:19:46,375 --> 01:19:49,375
(MST3K theme music)

2170
01:19:52,884 --> 01:19:54,737
- Who among you knows my mother?

2171
01:19:54,737 --> 01:19:56,749
- [Servo] He died.

2172
01:19:56,749 --> 01:20:00,662
- [Crow] Come on, people,
let's wake up in here!

2173
01:20:00,662 --> 01:20:03,608
- I know she is somewhere in this dungeon.

2174
01:20:03,608 --> 01:20:05,333
- [Servo] You're not
supposed to be on this floor.

2175
01:20:05,333 --> 01:20:08,087
- She has a small scar on her right cheek.

2176
01:20:08,087 --> 01:20:11,277
It is the remembrance of a Tougar sword.

2177
01:20:11,277 --> 01:20:13,123
- [Mike] I was a baby when I last saw her,

2178
01:20:13,123 --> 01:20:16,508
so I'll need to see all your breasts.

2179
01:20:16,508 --> 01:20:18,925
- [Crow] Are you Irene Papas?

2180
01:20:22,414 --> 01:20:23,509
- Mother.

2181
01:20:23,509 --> 01:20:24,733
Do not send me away.

2182
01:20:24,733 --> 01:20:25,566
Please forgive me.

2183
01:20:25,566 --> 01:20:26,646
- [Servo] Go watch TV.

2184
01:20:26,646 --> 01:20:27,479
- Please.

2185
01:20:29,553 --> 01:20:31,007
I have found my true father.

2186
01:20:31,007 --> 01:20:33,418
- [Servo] Did you follow
the trail of beer cans?

2187
01:20:33,418 --> 01:20:34,630
He sends you his love.

2188
01:20:34,630 --> 01:20:37,130
- [Crow] Did he sen any money?

2189
01:20:38,324 --> 01:20:41,048
(dramatic music)

2190
01:20:41,048 --> 01:20:41,888
- My boy!

2191
01:20:41,888 --> 01:20:45,195
- [Servo] You have a weird face.

2192
01:20:45,195 --> 01:20:46,028
- My boy.

2193
01:20:46,028 --> 01:20:48,795
- [Crow] I could really
use my boy right now.

2194
01:20:48,795 --> 01:20:50,133
(horde shouting)

2195
01:20:50,133 --> 01:20:52,020
- [Mike] Better check
that boat for mi-foil.

2196
01:20:52,020 --> 01:20:53,574
- [Crow] A rotten Trojan horse, there.

2197
01:20:53,574 --> 01:20:54,407
- Now we sail!

2198
01:20:54,407 --> 01:20:55,624
After them!

2199
01:20:55,624 --> 01:20:57,156
After the Tougars!

2200
01:20:57,156 --> 01:20:59,892
(swords clanging, shouting)

2201
01:20:59,892 --> 01:21:02,618
- [Crow] We fight for Dolly Madison!

2202
01:21:02,618 --> 01:21:05,711
- [Mike] Ah, everyone thought
to bring a light wrap.

2203
01:21:05,711 --> 01:21:06,807
(soldiers shouting)

2204
01:21:06,807 --> 01:21:08,696
- [Servo] Vroom, vroom, here we go.

2205
01:21:08,696 --> 01:21:09,779
Vroom, vroom!

2206
01:21:11,229 --> 01:21:14,229
- [Crow] Could someone invent water?

2207
01:21:16,012 --> 01:21:17,734
- [Mike] And still more Marias!

2208
01:21:17,734 --> 01:21:18,750
- [Servo] ♫ The hills are alive ♫

2209
01:21:18,750 --> 01:21:19,831
- To the mountain of Mertz!

2210
01:21:19,831 --> 01:21:21,135
Hurry!

2211
01:21:21,135 --> 01:21:22,589
- [Servo] I play at a gym!

2212
01:21:22,589 --> 01:21:26,448
- I wish to see the dregs of the enemy!

2213
01:21:26,448 --> 01:21:30,203
I must know the size of the
force he pits against me.

2214
01:21:30,203 --> 01:21:31,534
- [Crow] No need to explain, sir.

2215
01:21:31,534 --> 01:21:33,310
We like making mountains of men!

2216
01:21:33,310 --> 01:21:34,450
- Attack!

2217
01:21:34,450 --> 01:21:35,700
Higher, higher!

2218
01:21:36,552 --> 01:21:38,829
- [Servo] ♫ I wanna take you higher ♫

2219
01:21:38,829 --> 01:21:41,058
- [Mike] The trick here

2220
01:21:41,058 --> 01:21:43,095
is to be one of the last ones on the pile.

2221
01:21:43,095 --> 01:21:45,762
- [Servo] It's a Tougar pile-up!

2222
01:21:47,050 --> 01:21:48,771
Hey, you got my elbow in my groin.

2223
01:21:48,771 --> 01:21:51,181
- [Crow] I need to move my face.

2224
01:21:51,181 --> 01:21:52,378
- [Servo] What is that?

2225
01:21:52,378 --> 01:21:53,717
Ooh, it's soft!

2226
01:21:53,717 --> 01:21:55,221
- Come rally to my side, warriors!

2227
01:21:55,221 --> 01:21:59,352
And I will show you where Prince
Vanda and his cowards hide.

2228
01:21:59,352 --> 01:22:00,365
(horse neighing)

2229
01:22:00,365 --> 01:22:03,790
- I shall be the echo
responding to his call.

2230
01:22:03,790 --> 01:22:06,267
- [Mike] The first product
of the Acme company.

2231
01:22:06,267 --> 01:22:07,713
- [Crow] A-hah!

2232
01:22:07,713 --> 01:22:10,796
(soldier exclaiming)

2233
01:22:13,740 --> 01:22:14,573
(soldiers moaning)

2234
01:22:14,573 --> 01:22:15,659
- [Mike] My fillings!

2235
01:22:15,659 --> 01:22:16,492
- To the gate!

2236
01:22:16,492 --> 01:22:17,994
Release Zuma the fire dragon.

2237
01:22:17,994 --> 01:22:21,950
The palace will be nothing
but ashes and smoke!

2238
01:22:21,950 --> 01:22:24,420
- [Servo] Can we get up now?

2239
01:22:24,420 --> 01:22:28,343
- [Crow] It's Ghidorah!
(dragon's wings swooshing)

2240
01:22:28,343 --> 01:22:29,432
- [Mike] Okay, we're goin' left.

2241
01:22:29,432 --> 01:22:30,506
- [Servo] I say we're goin' right.

2242
01:22:30,506 --> 01:22:32,181
- [Crow] Would you two quit arguing?

2243
01:22:32,181 --> 01:22:33,189
I'll decide!

2244
01:22:33,189 --> 01:22:34,526
- [Mike] No, we're goin' left.

2245
01:22:34,526 --> 01:22:35,359
We're goin' left.

2246
01:22:35,359 --> 01:22:36,192
- [Servo] Shut up.

2247
01:22:36,192 --> 01:22:37,025
- Fire dragons!

2248
01:22:37,025 --> 01:22:37,926
They have released it!

2249
01:22:37,926 --> 01:22:38,807
- Go, Little Falcon.

2250
01:22:38,807 --> 01:22:40,595
You must go and help them now.

2251
01:22:40,595 --> 01:22:42,613
- No, I will not leave you here alone.

2252
01:22:42,613 --> 01:22:44,193
- No harm shall come to me.

2253
01:22:44,193 --> 01:22:47,725
I will find my way home safely, my son.

2254
01:22:47,725 --> 01:22:50,308
- [Servo] Admit it, we're lost.

2255
01:22:52,089 --> 01:22:52,922
(horde exclaiming)

2256
01:22:52,922 --> 01:22:53,755
- [Mike] This baby can handle

2257
01:22:53,755 --> 01:22:54,908
anything but a three-headed dra.

2258
01:22:54,908 --> 01:22:56,304
Oh, sonuva.

2259
01:22:56,304 --> 01:22:57,734
Aw!

2260
01:22:57,734 --> 01:22:59,586
(roaring)

2261
01:22:59,586 --> 01:23:01,092
(fleeing people screaming)

2262
01:23:01,092 --> 01:23:06,055
- [Servo] I love the smell
o'dragon breath in the morning.

2263
01:23:06,055 --> 01:23:07,648
- This dragon of theirs breathes fire,

2264
01:23:07,648 --> 01:23:09,021
but we'll extinguish him.

2265
01:23:09,021 --> 01:23:09,854
Look!

2266
01:23:09,854 --> 01:23:10,687
He flies like nightingale.

2267
01:23:10,687 --> 01:23:11,520
- [Crow] I heard that.

2268
01:23:11,520 --> 01:23:12,836
I do not fly like that.

2269
01:23:12,836 --> 01:23:15,669
(catapult firing)

2270
01:23:16,886 --> 01:23:18,625
- Look, the spear, it's hit him!

2271
01:23:18,625 --> 01:23:21,042
- [Mike] Help the bombardier.

2272
01:23:23,182 --> 01:23:24,563
(roaring)

2273
01:23:24,563 --> 01:23:25,620
- [Crow] I'll handle this guys.

2274
01:23:25,620 --> 01:23:26,864
- [Servo] Well, if you're sure.

2275
01:23:26,864 --> 01:23:28,424
- [Crow] Yeah, you two run along.

2276
01:23:28,424 --> 01:23:29,674
- [Servo] Okay.

2277
01:23:30,752 --> 01:23:33,578
(roaring)

2278
01:23:33,578 --> 01:23:36,655
- [Mike] Oh, the poor
little guy's just scared.

2279
01:23:36,655 --> 01:23:38,798
(roaring)

2280
01:23:38,798 --> 01:23:40,601
- [Servo] The whole
point of having a dragon

2281
01:23:40,601 --> 01:23:42,622
is telling the world
that you have a dragon.

2282
01:23:42,622 --> 01:23:45,039
Why did you keep it a secret?

2283
01:23:47,201 --> 01:23:48,034
(roaring)

2284
01:23:48,034 --> 01:23:49,129
- [Crow] Ah, shoot.
(exciting music)

2285
01:23:49,129 --> 01:23:50,310
I just waxed that boat!

2286
01:23:50,310 --> 01:23:52,163
(metal clanging)

2287
01:23:52,163 --> 01:23:54,765
- [Mike] I love my job.

2288
01:23:54,765 --> 01:23:56,219
- The prince shall be killed.

2289
01:23:56,219 --> 01:23:59,304
When we are the victors, Morometz dies.

2290
01:23:59,304 --> 01:24:01,946
He shall be burned alive.

2291
01:24:01,946 --> 01:24:03,962
(roaring)

2292
01:24:03,962 --> 01:24:07,545
- [Crow] Dragonslayer
II, the uncalled for.

2293
01:24:09,800 --> 01:24:10,863
(roaring)

2294
01:24:10,863 --> 01:24:13,207
(Crow, Mike and Servo emulating sirens)

2295
01:24:13,207 --> 01:24:15,874
- August Strindberg's Backdraft.

2296
01:24:18,262 --> 01:24:20,624
- [Servo] Now for the
best part of my plan.

2297
01:24:20,624 --> 01:24:21,457
Retreat!

2298
01:24:22,999 --> 01:24:24,404
(exciting music)

2299
01:24:24,404 --> 01:24:28,003
- [Crow] Woo, get that dragon
the world's biggest mint.

2300
01:24:28,003 --> 01:24:29,503
- [Mike] Oy-oy-oy.

2301
01:24:31,438 --> 01:24:32,271
(catapult firing)

2302
01:24:32,271 --> 01:24:33,938
- [Servo] Thank you!

2303
01:24:34,970 --> 01:24:36,159
- [Crow] Hello, I'm on fire!

2304
01:24:36,159 --> 01:24:36,992
Help!

2305
01:24:36,992 --> 01:24:39,017
- Take that, firey dragon!

2306
01:24:39,017 --> 01:24:40,404
Oh, his breath.

2307
01:24:40,404 --> 01:24:42,412
This is like our oven.

2308
01:24:42,412 --> 01:24:44,963
- [Servo] Hi, can I help you?

2309
01:24:44,963 --> 01:24:45,796
Aagh!

2310
01:24:48,976 --> 01:24:49,809
(swords claning)

2311
01:24:49,809 --> 01:24:53,329
- [Crow] Is someone putting
away the silverware?

2312
01:24:53,329 --> 01:24:55,641
- Father, together we shall
send this firey monster

2313
01:24:55,641 --> 01:24:57,676
back to the hell he came from!

2314
01:24:57,676 --> 01:24:59,214
- [Mike] Little Thelonius Falcon,

2315
01:24:59,214 --> 01:25:01,232
you can down from there right now!

2316
01:25:01,232 --> 01:25:04,565
- [Servo] Why do I always have to carve?

2317
01:25:06,505 --> 01:25:07,338
- Water!

2318
01:25:08,365 --> 01:25:10,032
- [Crow] Not for me!

2319
01:25:13,999 --> 01:25:15,986
- Dragon head, already!

2320
01:25:15,986 --> 01:25:17,269
- [Mike] We'll be eating dragon sandwiches

2321
01:25:17,269 --> 01:25:19,567
for the next month. (smacking lips)

2322
01:25:19,567 --> 01:25:20,738
- Follow me, warriors!

2323
01:25:20,738 --> 01:25:22,219
The enemy is in retreat!

2324
01:25:22,219 --> 01:25:24,264
We shall drive them into the sea!

2325
01:25:24,264 --> 01:25:27,873
- [Crow] Horse looks like Stallone.

2326
01:25:27,873 --> 01:25:29,831
(soldiers exclaiming, exciting music)

2327
01:25:29,831 --> 01:25:33,927
- [Servo] Ilya's plan is still
being taught at West Point.

2328
01:25:33,927 --> 01:25:36,867
- [Crow] Gee, the sky is
as clear as Gary, Indiana.

2329
01:25:36,867 --> 01:25:38,977
(Servo coughing)

2330
01:25:38,977 --> 01:25:39,867
- [Mike] You know,

2331
01:25:39,867 --> 01:25:43,853
now I have an unhealthy
hatred of Finnish people.

2332
01:25:43,853 --> 01:25:44,895
- [Servo] I suppose, huh?

2333
01:25:44,895 --> 01:25:45,728
- [Mike] Ah, yeah.

2334
01:25:45,728 --> 01:25:47,404
We've been on it quite a while.

2335
01:25:47,404 --> 01:25:50,987
Time to get back home.
- [Crow] Miller time.

2336
01:25:53,140 --> 01:25:54,274
- [Servo] If you don't
wanna ride those horses,

2337
01:25:54,274 --> 01:25:56,205
you could take the fjord. (chuckling)

2338
01:25:56,205 --> 01:25:58,415
- [Mike] Should we make a big mountain?

2339
01:25:58,415 --> 01:26:01,571
- [Crow] No, we don't have
to make a big mountain.

2340
01:26:01,571 --> 01:26:02,451
- [Mike] I was just asking.

2341
01:26:02,451 --> 01:26:03,358
Fine.

2342
01:26:03,358 --> 01:26:06,979
(exclaiming, gong clanging)

2343
01:26:06,979 --> 01:26:07,979
- Foxy lady.

2344
01:26:09,359 --> 01:26:10,192
- Fight!

2345
01:26:11,126 --> 01:26:12,024
Fight, cowards, fight!

2346
01:26:12,024 --> 01:26:15,241
Sons of battle, listen to my oath.

2347
01:26:15,241 --> 01:26:17,169
Spare me and I shall save you.

2348
01:26:17,169 --> 01:26:18,002
I promise you this.

2349
01:26:18,002 --> 01:26:18,838
(exclaiming)

2350
01:26:18,838 --> 01:26:20,612
- [Crow] Ooh, is there a dipping sauce?

2351
01:26:20,612 --> 01:26:23,873
- Prepare to die, soldier for Kalin.

2352
01:26:23,873 --> 01:26:25,670
- Spare me, I beg of you.

2353
01:26:25,670 --> 01:26:27,034
Be merciful.

2354
01:26:27,034 --> 01:26:29,146
Spare a handful of Tougars, please,

2355
01:26:29,146 --> 01:26:30,896
so we may beget sons.

2356
01:26:31,837 --> 01:26:33,439
- Steady your hand, warrior!

2357
01:26:33,439 --> 01:26:36,410
Our people shall judge the fate of Kalin.

2358
01:26:36,410 --> 01:26:38,885
- Let us take him alive to the palace.

2359
01:26:38,885 --> 01:26:40,563
Treat him like the cur that he is.

2360
01:26:40,563 --> 01:26:43,031
Stuff him in a sack and
take him back to the palace.

2361
01:26:43,031 --> 01:26:44,204
(laughing)

2362
01:26:44,204 --> 01:26:46,660
- [Mike] Those guys are so
funny at times like this.

2363
01:26:46,660 --> 01:26:50,410
- [Servo] Well, if you
can laugh once at war.

2364
01:26:51,799 --> 01:26:53,963
(laughter)

2365
01:26:53,963 --> 01:26:57,331
- And so ends the Mighty Chief Kalin.

2366
01:26:57,331 --> 01:27:01,498
- [Servo] ♫ The hills are in flames ♫

2367
01:27:03,248 --> 01:27:05,998
(dramatic music)

2368
01:27:07,563 --> 01:27:08,896
- Ilya, my love!

2369
01:27:10,005 --> 01:27:11,419
- [Crow] I have some things to explain

2370
01:27:11,419 --> 01:27:13,271
about me and the wind demon.

2371
01:27:13,271 --> 01:27:15,533
- Delia, my dearest.

2372
01:27:15,533 --> 01:27:16,829
- [Mike] I wanna feel ya, Ilya.

2373
01:27:16,829 --> 01:27:19,170
- At last I have found you.

2374
01:27:19,170 --> 01:27:21,153
(dramatic music)

2375
01:27:21,153 --> 01:27:24,448
- [Servo] Hey, they captured Billy Barty!

2376
01:27:24,448 --> 01:27:26,173
(dramatic music)

2377
01:27:26,173 --> 01:27:28,196
- [Mike] Oh, it's housing project hill.

2378
01:27:28,196 --> 01:27:30,159
- [Crow] I have Rockports.

2379
01:27:30,159 --> 01:27:32,084
- In your honor, Ilya,

2380
01:27:32,084 --> 01:27:33,802
we shall have a feast.

2381
01:27:33,802 --> 01:27:35,458
- [Mike] Now get back to the dungeon, you.

2382
01:27:35,458 --> 01:27:38,815
- Henceforth, Ilya, you
shall live in the palace.

2383
01:27:38,815 --> 01:27:40,851
You shall become a noble or a prince.

2384
01:27:40,851 --> 01:27:41,825
- [Servo] Or something.

2385
01:27:41,825 --> 01:27:44,483
- Thank you my prince, but I
could not live at the palace.

2386
01:27:44,483 --> 01:27:45,456
- [Crow] It stinks in there.

2387
01:27:45,456 --> 01:27:47,276
- I must pursue my destiny.

2388
01:27:47,276 --> 01:27:49,521
I must go where adventure leads me.

2389
01:27:49,521 --> 01:27:50,875
- [Servo] I'm joining the Hogan tour.

2390
01:27:50,875 --> 01:27:53,501
- The road to life has
many different pasts.

2391
01:27:53,501 --> 01:27:54,334
This brave

2392
01:27:54,334 --> 01:27:55,514
and willing soldier.
- [Mike] Ow!

2393
01:27:55,514 --> 01:27:58,347
- He will serve you well at court.

2394
01:27:59,645 --> 01:28:01,530
He is my son.

2395
01:28:01,530 --> 01:28:02,447
- So be it.

2396
01:28:03,301 --> 01:28:04,898
We shall be proud to have with us

2397
01:28:04,898 --> 01:28:07,141
the son of Ilya Morometz.

2398
01:28:07,141 --> 01:28:08,982
- [Crow] Even though
he is a Mongol bastard.

2399
01:28:08,982 --> 01:28:09,994
- Bring no dishonor

2400
01:28:09,994 --> 01:28:13,201
on the magic sword of Invincor.

2401
01:28:13,201 --> 01:28:15,868
- [Mike] Gee, Dad, it's a daisy.

2402
01:28:17,165 --> 01:28:18,170
- [Servo] Ow!

2403
01:28:18,170 --> 01:28:19,335
I cut myself

2404
01:28:19,335 --> 01:28:20,905
- I accept this sword.

2405
01:28:20,905 --> 01:28:24,403
And I shall honor it always, Father.

2406
01:28:24,403 --> 01:28:26,949
- Bravo, Ilya Morometz, bravo!

2407
01:28:26,949 --> 01:28:28,310
- [Crowd] Bravo, Ilya Morometz!

2408
01:28:28,310 --> 01:28:31,095
- [Servo] His son did bring dishonor.

2409
01:28:31,095 --> 01:28:32,752
He traded the sword for a lid

2410
01:28:32,752 --> 01:28:34,311
and got high in the palace.

2411
01:28:34,311 --> 01:28:35,392
(Mike laughing)

2412
01:28:35,392 --> 01:28:37,278
- [Crow] ♫ So long, country bumpkin

2413
01:28:37,278 --> 01:28:41,480
♫ Fresh as frost down on the pumpkin ♫

2414
01:28:41,480 --> 01:28:44,980
(metal clanging, beeping)

2415
01:28:52,797 --> 01:28:55,830
- You hear Kate Mulgrew is Mrs. Pickard?

2416
01:28:55,830 --> 01:28:56,993
- [Crow] Yes, that's--

2417
01:28:56,993 --> 01:28:57,826
- Hey, guys!

2418
01:28:57,826 --> 01:28:58,680
I got ahold of the first edition

2419
01:28:58,680 --> 01:29:01,456
of Gypsy's review of our
political satirical revue.

2420
01:29:01,456 --> 01:29:02,289
- Oh, yeah!

2421
01:29:02,289 --> 01:29:03,122
- Oh, don't read that stuff.

2422
01:29:03,122 --> 01:29:04,664
Why feel bad if you don't have to?

2423
01:29:04,664 --> 01:29:05,497
Huh?

2424
01:29:05,497 --> 01:29:06,330
- Come on, Mike.

2425
01:29:06,330 --> 01:29:07,163
I'm sure you got a mention.

2426
01:29:07,163 --> 01:29:07,996
Now, let's take a look here.

2427
01:29:07,996 --> 01:29:10,161
All righty, here goes.

2428
01:29:10,161 --> 01:29:13,199
As I watched
Supercalifragilisticexpiali-wacky,

2429
01:29:13,199 --> 01:29:15,118
one question clawed at my brain.

2430
01:29:15,118 --> 01:29:18,467
Does such delight actually
dwell in the universe?

2431
01:29:18,467 --> 01:29:19,638
Here it comes.

2432
01:29:19,638 --> 01:29:21,591
The answer is yes, yes, yes.

2433
01:29:21,591 --> 01:29:22,424
Hey!

2434
01:29:22,424 --> 01:29:25,024
And it comes in a big, blond
package called Mike Nelson!

2435
01:29:25,024 --> 01:29:26,478
- Hey, yeah.
- [Servo] There you go.

2436
01:29:26,478 --> 01:29:27,651
Bright and irreverent,

2437
01:29:27,651 --> 01:29:30,576
Mr. Nelson thrills the viewer
with his charismatic presence.

2438
01:29:30,576 --> 01:29:32,530
Ha ha, what a treat this man is.

2439
01:29:32,530 --> 01:29:33,725
- Wow.

2440
01:29:33,725 --> 01:29:36,970
- Mr. Servo, however, bounded on the.

2441
01:29:36,970 --> 01:29:37,975
- Yeah?

2442
01:29:37,975 --> 01:29:38,808
- Yeah?

2443
01:29:39,928 --> 01:29:42,739
- Um, (clearing throat)
Mr. Servo, however,

2444
01:29:42,739 --> 01:29:44,791
bounded on stage, shrieking his lines,

2445
01:29:44,791 --> 01:29:46,928
shrill as a fishwife.

2446
01:29:46,928 --> 01:29:50,335
Who or what put this man on stage?

2447
01:29:50,335 --> 01:29:51,983
Brr.

2448
01:29:51,983 --> 01:29:54,523
Uh, Crow T. Robot rounds out the cast.

2449
01:29:54,523 --> 01:29:56,947
- Well, hey, you really
did round out he cast!

2450
01:29:56,947 --> 01:29:57,780
- I did?

2451
01:29:57,780 --> 01:29:58,613
- Yeah.

2452
01:29:58,613 --> 01:29:59,446
- All right!

2453
01:29:59,446 --> 01:30:00,809
- Yeah, and you, I mean, a fishwife.

2454
01:30:00,809 --> 01:30:02,219
That's good.

2455
01:30:02,219 --> 01:30:03,052
That's good.

2456
01:30:03,052 --> 01:30:05,687
Because what is a
fishwife, but chopped fish.

2457
01:30:05,687 --> 01:30:09,354
Hey, look, the things,
the guys are calling.

2458
01:30:14,888 --> 01:30:15,794
- Hey, Nelstoney, ha.

2459
01:30:15,794 --> 01:30:17,225
You probably noticed

2460
01:30:17,225 --> 01:30:18,588
all the skirts running
around down here. (chuckling)

2461
01:30:18,588 --> 01:30:19,543
The place was lousy with 'em.

2462
01:30:19,543 --> 01:30:20,442
Well, they're gone now,

2463
01:30:20,442 --> 01:30:23,192
but if they were still here, hoo.

2464
01:30:24,158 --> 01:30:25,680
(both chuckling)

2465
01:30:25,680 --> 01:30:26,903
- Yep, there are four words

2466
01:30:26,903 --> 01:30:29,526
to describe the climate down here.

2467
01:30:29,526 --> 01:30:30,693
Va-va-va-voom!

2468
01:30:32,791 --> 01:30:34,224
(both chuckling)

2469
01:30:34,224 --> 01:30:35,096
You know, Clay,

2470
01:30:35,096 --> 01:30:37,851
you and I should go cruisin'
for some more lady love.

2471
01:30:37,851 --> 01:30:39,714
- Ah, no doubt, no doubt, Frankie.

2472
01:30:39,714 --> 01:30:40,777
But, uh.

2473
01:30:40,777 --> 01:30:43,337
I've gotta bag up the rest
of my Animal Man collection.

2474
01:30:43,337 --> 01:30:44,904
If it weren't for that.

2475
01:30:44,904 --> 01:30:46,454
Pa-poom!

2476
01:30:46,454 --> 01:30:48,839
- Understood, my friend, understood.

2477
01:30:48,839 --> 01:30:50,170
It's like me.

2478
01:30:50,170 --> 01:30:53,511
Right now I'd go out cruisin'
for some more lady love,

2479
01:30:53,511 --> 01:30:57,356
but there are three very
good reasons why I can't.

2480
01:30:57,356 --> 01:30:59,189
Universal Action Pack.

2481
01:31:01,754 --> 01:31:05,837
(phone ringing, both exclaiming)

2482
01:31:10,812 --> 01:31:14,229
("The MST3K Love Theme")

